window.SIGNIN_CHAPTERS=(window.SIGNIN_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: Universal Sign-In System","paragraphs":["Jude stood by the reception podium, his hands clasped behind his back.","\"Welcome,\" Jude said, forcing a customer-service smile onto his face as two figures stepped over the threshold. \"How may I—\"","A woman in a stunning designer dress walked into the showroom, a pair of oversized luxury sunglasses perched on her styled hair.","Hanging off her arm was a young man wearing a casual outfit that probably cost more than Jude’s yearly salary, a bored expression across his face.","It was Chloe. His ex-fiancée.","Chloe paused, lowering her sunglasses slightly to peer at the employee greeting them.","For a brief second, shock registered on her face, quickly followed by a twisted smirk.","\"Well, well, well,\" Chloe chuckled. \"Oh, how the mighty have fallen. From dreaming big to greeting real men at the door...\"","The few affluent customers browsing the floor turned their heads, their brows furrowing at the sudden disturbance.","The young man next to her let out a breath of amusement, adjusting his watch. \"Who is this, babe? A friend of yours?\"","\"Hardly,\" Chloe scoffed, taking a step forward to look Jude up and down with disgust. \"Trent, this is Jude. The loser I told you about. The one who thought he could marry me while struggling to pay rent in a shoebox apartment.\"","Jude felt his chest tighten but he kept his hands clasped behind his back. He dug his nails into his palms to maintain his composure.","\"Ma’am, if you are here to view our collection, I would be happy to assign a senior specialist to guide you,\" Jude said.","\"Ma’am?\" Chloe repeated. She turned to Trent, laughing. \"Did you hear that? Just look at him, Trent. Look at that pathetic suit. He doesn’t even belong in the same zip code as these cars, let alone inside this building.\"","\"It is quite the eyesore,\" Trent agreed lazily. \"Makes me question the standards of this establishment.\"","Jude’s jaw clenched. The muscles in his neck jumped, but he swallowed his pride.","He needed this job. He was already drowning in debt, and losing a position at a high-end dealership would be the final nail in his financial coffin.","\"If there is no specific vehicle you wish to see,\" Jude managed to say, \"I kindly ask that you keep your voices down for the comfort of the other clients.\"","\"Oh, giving orders now?\" Chloe’s eyes flashed with cruel delight. She let go of Trent’s arm and strutted directly up to Jude, jabbing a finger toward a sports car parked on the center display.","It was the newly imported Zenith V12, carrying a price tag of over three million dollars.","\"You want to talk about vehicles, Jude? Fine,\" Chloe sneered. \"Buy that one.\"","Jude stared at her, his expression tight. \"Excuse me?\"","\"You heard me,\" she challenged, stepping even closer so the showroom could hear her declaration. \"You always talked big when we were together. Always said you were going to make it, that you just needed time. Well, here’s your chance. Buy the Zenith. If you have even an ounce of manhood left in that pathetic body of yours, put down the cash and buy it right now.\"","Whispers broke out among the onlookers.","A few staff members had gathered near the offices, watching the spectacle with wide eyes, whispering to each other.","Jude stood silent. He couldn’t buy a tire on that car, let alone the vehicle itself.","He had exactly $42 in his checking account. Chloe knew this. She knew exactly how utterly destroyed his finances were because she was the one who had drained their joint savings before abandoning him.","\"Nothing to say?\" Chloe laughed, turning back to Trent. \"See? I told you. All bark, completely hollow on the inside. Just a broke, useless—\"","\"What is the meaning of this?!\" a voice shouted from the back of the showroom.","Mr. Sterling, the general manager, came sprinting across the floor.","His face was flushed red, and he was sweating profusely as he shoved his way past Jude.","\"Mr. Sterling,\" Jude started. \"These guests were just—\"","\"Shut your mouth!\" Mr. Sterling barked at Jude before spinning around to face Trent.","The manager’s posture immediately hunched into a bow. \"Mr. Belmont! I am so incredibly sorry! I didn’t realize the Belmont family heir was gracing our showroom today. If I had known, I would have cleared the floor for you!\"","Trent waved a hand. \"Your hospitality is lacking, Sterling. I come here to browse for a new toy, and my girlfriend is forced to interact with this trash. It really ruins the prestigious image you claim to have.\"","Mr. Sterling turned deathly pale. The Belmont family owned half the real estate in the city; offending Trent was akin to career suicide.","The manager whipped his head toward Jude, his eyes burning with fury.","\"Jude, you incompetent fool!\" Mr. Sterling roared, not caring who heard him. \"How dare you disrespect our most esteemed VIPs? Look at yourself! You look like a beggar who wandered in from the slums! I told you to stay in the back and clean the glass, not interact with the clients!\"","\"Mr. Sterling, I was simply standing at the podium. She approached me and—\"","\"I said shut up!\" the manager screamed, his spit flying onto Jude’s lapel. \"Pack your things, leave your uniform in the breakroom, and get out of my sight. You’re fired! And don’t even think about asking for this week’s paycheck to cover the damage you’ve done to our reputation!\"","Jude looked from the red-faced manager to Trent, who was smirking in victory, and finally to Chloe, who was glowing with satisfaction.","The injustice of it burned in Jude’s chest like swallowed coals. He wanted to throw a punch. He wanted to scream at the ridiculous unfairness of a world where the wealthy could casually destroy a man’s livelihood just for a fleeting moment of entertainment.","But he didn’t.","Because what would it accomplish? He had no power. He had no backing. If he fought back, Trent could have him thrown in a cell by the end of the hour, and no lawyer would ever take his case.","Without a single word, Jude untied his company tie, draped it over the reception podium, and turned his back on them.","He walked past the hypercars and pushed open the doors.","Jude walked down the busy sidewalk, ignoring the throngs of wealthy pedestrians passing him by.","He kept his head down.","What was the point of playing by the rules?","He had worked seventy-hour weeks. He had smiled at the insults. He had swallowed his pride every single day, hoping that hard work and decency would eventually pay off. But the reality of the world was far colder.","In this society, if you didn’t have money or a powerful background, you were just an NPC in someone else’s game.","You were dirt meant to be stepped on so the rich could keep their shoes clean.","He stopped walking and leaned against a wall, letting out a long sigh.","He closed his eyes, wondering how he was going to explain the eviction notice on his door to the landlord now that his sole source of income was gone.","Suddenly, a sound echoed inside his skull.","[Ding!]","Jude snapped his eyes open, looking wildly around the empty alleyway. \"Who’s there?\"","[The Universal Sign-In System has successfully initiated. Would you like to bind with the System?]","Jude froze. \"A system? What... what are you? Am I hallucinating?\"","[I am the Universal Sign-In System,]","[I am an auxiliary interface designed to elevate the host’s status across all measurable metrics. By signing in daily at designated locations, the host will be rewarded with limitless wealth, peerless skills, rare items, and physical enhancements. The more prestigious the location of the sign-in, the more extraordinary the reward. Through me, the host can conquer the world.]","Jude stared blankly at the wall opposite him. Unparalleled wealth? Skills? Status?","Everything he had just been despairing over was being handed to him on a silver platter by a voice in his head.","He hesitated. Was the stress finally breaking his mind? Was he standing in an alleyway, having a psychotic break from the trauma of losing his job and being humiliated?","Yet, as he stood there, feeling the bite of his cheap shoes and remembering the mocking laughter of those who thought they owned the world, his hesitation dissolved.","If he was crazy, so be it.","If this was real... if this was his one chance to flip the board and crush the people who looked down on him, how could he ever walk away?","[Would you like to sign in?]"]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: A New Feature","paragraphs":["Jude swallowed hard, his throat dry. He looked back toward the glass doors of the dealership where his entire life had just been dismantled.","\"Yes,\" Jude whispered, his voice trembling slightly. \"Sign in.\"","[Ding! First Sign-In successfully registered.]","[Location: Zenith Motors Service Alley.]","[Location Evaluation: Very Low.]","[However, First-Time Sign-In Bonus applied!]","[Reward: $10,000,000 USD.]","Jude stopped breathing.","His phone vibrated in his pocket. He pulled it out with shaky fingers and stared at the screen.","It was a push notification from his banking app... an account that had sat at a depressing forty-two dollars for the past two weeks.","Apex National Bank: Direct Deposit Received.","Available Balance: $10,000,042.00.","Jude wiped his eyes, thinking his vision was blurring.","He unlocked the phone, opened the app, and stared at the dashboard. He counted the zeros.","One, two, three... six zeros. Ten million dollars. He refreshed the application. He closed it completely and launched it again.","The numbers stared back at him.","The unpaid bills, the threat of eviction, the endless agonizing over grocery prices evaporated in a single heartbeat.","Jude let out a breathless laugh, leaning the back of his head against the wall.","He shoved the phone back into his pocket and walked toward the main street.","Just as he rounded the corner to the sidewalk, a voice called out from behind him.","\"Hey. Jude, wait up.\"","Jude turned. Walking toward him was Derek, one of the junior sales associates from the dealership.","Derek had a black trash bag in one hand, having clearly been sent out to do the grunt work.","Derek dropped the bag by the curb and wiped his hands on his slacks, his posture hesitant. He looked Jude up and down, offering a soft, almost pitying smile.","\"Listen, man,\" Derek started, stepping a little closer. \"I’m sorry about what happened in there. Sterling is a tyrant, and that Trent guy... well, he’s a jerk. I didn’t want to say anything inside, you know, to keep my job, but it was really messed up.\"","Jude blinked, momentarily caught off guard.","He had expected Derek to throw out a sarcastic comment or laugh at his expense. But sympathy? That was unexpected.","Still, Jude didn’t feel any of the lingering anger he had felt inside the building. It was hard to be angry when you had ten million dollars sitting in your pocket.","\"It’s fine, Derek,\" Jude said with a relaxed smile, and turned to resume walking down the block.","\"Wait, hold on!\" Derek jogged a few steps to catch up.","Jude paused, raising an eyebrow.","Derek dug into his wallet, trying his best to look helpful, but Jude could see the burning curiosity in his eyes.","Derek wanted to know what the ’ruined’ guy was going to do next.","\"I know things are tight,\" Derek said, pulling out a crumpled fifty-dollar bill and extending it. \"With Chloe draining your accounts and now losing this gig... take this. Get a hot meal. And hey, if you need a reference for a warehouse job or something, let me know. What are you going to do now?\"","Jude didn’t answer right away. He looked at the fifty-dollar bill, then up at Derek’s expectant face.","A few hours ago, Jude might have swallowed his pride and taken the cash just to survive the week.","Now, he just found the situation incredibly amusing...","Jude gently pushed Derek’s hand back. \"Keep it, Derek,\" he said simply. \"You’re going to need it for the new car payments you were complaining about yesterday.\"","Derek blinked. \"Are you sure? Man, you don’t have a job.\"","\"I’ll manage,\" Jude chuckled softly.","He didn’t explain further. He just gave Derek a confident nod and walked away.","Derek stood on the sidewalk, watching Jude go. He had fully expected Jude to break down crying, or at least look panicked. Instead, the guy looked like he had just won the lottery. Derek shook his head, thoroughly confused, and walked back to the dealership.","...","Instead of heading toward the subway station to take the train back to his cramped apartment, Jude walked to the edge of the busy avenue and raised his hand.","A sleek, black premium cab pulled over. Jude slid into the backseat.","\"Where to, buddy?\" the driver asked, eyeing Jude’s cheap, slightly wrinkled suit through the rearview mirror.","\"The Obsidian Grand,\" Jude replied, his tone smooth.","The driver raised an eyebrow. The Obsidian Grand was a seven-star luxury hotel in the heart of the financial district, famous for hosting foreign diplomats, celebrities, and billionaires.","\"You sure about that, pal? It’s on the other side of town. Meter ticks fast.\"","\"I’m sure,\" Jude said, leaning back and crossing his legs.","The drive took twenty-five minutes. When they pulled up to the glittering, gold-trimmed entrance of the towering hotel, Jude opened his banking app, linked it to his digital wallet, and tapped his phone against the driver’s payment terminal.","He added a five-hundred-dollar tip.","The driver’s jaw unhinged when he saw the receipt print out. \"S-Sir! Thank you! Have a wonderful night!\"","Jude stepped out onto the red carpet. The doorman, impeccably dressed in a tailored uniform, hesitated for a fraction of a second upon seeing Jude’s attire, but his elite training took over. He pulled the doors open with a respectful bow.","He walked straight to the front desk. The receptionist, a stunning woman with perfectly pinned hair, offered a polite smile.","\"Welcome to the Obsidian Grand, sir. How may I assist you?\"","\"I need a room,\" Jude said casually. \"Your best available suite.\"","The receptionist paused, her fingers hovering over her keyboard.","She did a quick, subtle sweep of his frayed collar and scuffed shoes.","\"Sir, our luxury suites start at five thousand dollars a night. Furthermore, we require a substantial incidental deposit upfront...\"","\"The Presidential Suite. Book it for a month,\" Jude interrupted.","He tapped his phone against the platinum reader on the desk.","The receptionist’s eyes widened as the terminal chimed instantly.","A month in the Presidential Suite, plus the deposit, came out to over $180,000!","She fully expected the machine to flash red with a loud decline.","*Approved.*","The green text lit up her face. Her demeanor changed instantly.","\"R-Right away, Mr. Jude,\" she stammered, standing up a little straighter. \"I apologize for any delay. I will have our head concierge escort you to the top floor immediately. Shall we send up a tailor? Or perhaps arrange for room service?\"","\"Both,\" Jude said.","Not long after, Jude was standing inside a living space larger than the entire car dealership he used to work at.","Floor-to-ceiling windows offered a panoramic view of the sparkling city skyline. There was a private bar, a grand piano, and a bathroom encased in black marble.","He ordered food. Wagyu steak cooked rare, butter-poached lobster, truffle risotto, and a bottle of vintage wine.","When the food arrived, wheeled in on silver carts by bowing staff, Jude sat alone at the dining table. He plated the food carefully.","Each bite tasted better than the last.","For the first time in his adult life, Jude was eating because he wanted to.","The rest of the evening drifted by like a dream...","He took a long, steaming shower in the jacuzzi tub, letting the jets wash away the sweat, and the humiliation of the day.","He put on a ridiculously soft silk bathrobe, poured himself a glass of cold juice from the minibar, and reclined on the king-sized bed.","*So this is how the top one percent lives,* Jude thought, staring out at the city lights.","Jude stared at the ceiling, his heart rate picking up.","What about the system? He hadn’t heard the voice since the alleyway.","What if the system vanished tomorrow?","Sure, ten million was a lot of money, but what if that was it? What if he woke up tomorrow and the magic was gone?","The anxiety gnawed at him. The thought of losing this feeling, of ever having to go back to begging for scraps or being looked down on by people like Trent, made his chest tighten painfully.","He was just about to sit up and try speaking to the system out loud, desperate for an answer, when a chime echoed in his skull.","[Ding!]","[A new day has arrived. Would the host like to Sign-In?]","Jude sat up so fast he nearly spilled his juice. A relieved grin broke out across his face.","\"Yes,\" Jude said to the empty room.","[Sign-In Successful! Location: Obsidian Grand Hotel, Presidential Suite.]","[Location Evaluation: Very High.]","[Reward: $3,000,000 USD, +5 Attribute Points.]","[The Host has accumulated enough rewards to unlock the System Interface.]","[To view your current standing and allocate points, please say ’Status’.]","His phone buzzed on the nightstand almost immediately.","Jude grabbed it, opened the banking app, and laughed out loud when he saw the new balance."]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: Buying Respect","paragraphs":["\"Status,\" Jude said aloud.","A panel immediately materialized in the air in front of him. It hovered just above the edge of his bed.","[Host: Jude Lawson]","[Wealth: $12,820,042.00]","[Physical Attributes]","- Strength: 15","- Agility: 12","- Endurance: 14","*(Note: Average Adult Male is 10)*","[Available Attribute Points: 5]","[Inventory: Platinum VIP Shopping Card x1]","Jude stared at the text. Physical attributes? He didn’t hesitate. He allocated three points to Strength and two to Agility.","The moment he confirmed the selection, a rush of searing heat washed over his body.","His muscles tensed, expanding slightly under his skin, and his vision sharpened to a razor’s edge.","The dull ache in his lower back vanished completely. He felt lighter, stronger, and more alive than he had in a decade.","He slept like the dead that night.","The next morning, Jude stood in front of the floor-to-ceiling mirror in his suite. He was still wearing the same cheap suit he had been fired in. It was out of place in the lavish surroundings of the Obsidian Grand.","If he was going to live like a king, he needed to look the part.","After a massive room-service breakfast, Jude took the hotel’s complimentary town car to the Zenith District, a high-end shopping avenue lined with flagship designer stores.","He stepped out in front of *Aurelius*, a hyper-exclusive menswear boutique renowned for dressing A-list actors and billionaire tech moguls.","Three impeccably dressed employees were standing near the cashmere display. They took one collective look at Jude’s scuffed shoes, frayed lapels, and off-the-rack shirt. Instantly, they looked away, resuming their conversation as if he were invisible.","To them, it was obvious. Jude was either a lost tourist or a nobody hoping to snap a quick photo for social media. He certainly didn’t belong in a store where a simple leather belt cost more than his car.","Jude ignored their blatant dismissal and began browsing the racks.","His eyes landed on a stunning midnight-blue bespoke blazer displayed on a velvet mannequin. He reached out to feel the material.","\"Excuse me,\" Jude called out, waving a hand toward the group of employees. \"Could I get some assistance over here?\"","One of the men, a tall stylist with a trimmed beard and a nametag that read *Julian*, let out a quiet sigh.","He reluctantly detached himself from his colleagues and strolled over, his expression carefully wiped of everything except boredom.","\"Yes?\" Julian asked, not bothering to offer a greeting.","\"I like the cut of this blazer,\" Jude said, gesturing to the mannequin. \"What are my options for a full suit in this style?\"","Julian offered a tight smile. \"For a full suit? Sir, that particular piece is crafted from vicuña wool. It is our most exclusive seasonal item. The blazer alone is twenty-two thousand dollars.\"","\"I didn’t ask the price,\" Jude said mildly. \"I asked what my options were.\"","Julian let out a short, condescending laugh. \"Look, let me be blunt so we don’t waste each other’s time. We don’t offer payment plans. We don’t have a discount rack. If you’re looking for something affordable for a job interview, there’s a department store three blocks down the street.\"","Jude frowned. He had spent years working in high-end retail, and he knew exactly how much pressure there was to qualify customers. But this wasn’t qualifying; this was just blatant disrespect.","\"I asked a simple question about the suit,\" Jude said. \"Does my question mean I can’t afford it?\"","\"Your clothes mean you can’t afford it,\" Julian snapped. He looked Jude up and down with open disgust. \"You walked into a boutique wearing a polyester suit that looks like it was dug out of a donation bin. Do you honestly expect me to treat you like a VIP?\"","A few other customers in the store glanced over, their brows furrowing at the commotion, but Julian didn’t seem to care. He crossed his arms.","\"It’s your job to assist customers,\" Jude said. \"If you don’t want to do your job, I suggest you hand over your measuring tape and go home.\"","Julian’s face flushed with anger. \"Are you kidding me? Why should I waste my morning humoring a broke window-shopper? If I don’t like the look of someone who clearly can’t afford our inventory, I don’t have to serve them!\"","Jude glanced at the other two employees. They were watching the scene with indifferent expressions, making zero effort to step in or de-escalate.","\"Fine,\" Jude said, shaking his head. He pointed at the midnight-blue display. \"I want that suit. Complete set. Shirt, tie, trousers, blazer. The highest-tier fabric you have in the back. Bring it out.\"","Julian sneered, rolling his eyes. \"Who are you trying to impress, man? A full bespoke set from that line is thirty-five thousand dollars. Plus tax. You want me to ring it up? Prove you can pay for it first.\"","Jude didn’t say a word. He reached into his pocket and pulled out the Platinum VIP Shopping Card the system had rewarded him with last night.","He tossed it onto the display counter.","Julian stared at the card. He had never seen one quite like it, but it looked expensive. Still, he was convinced this was a bluff. The guy was probably trying to max out five different credit cards just to save face.","\"Alright,\" Julian said. \"If you want to play games and embarrass yourself, follow me to the register.\"","Julian marched over to the main terminal, punched in the total for the flagship set, and snatched the Platinum card off the counter.","He slammed it against the contactless reader, fully expecting the machine to scream *DECLINED* so he could happily kick Jude out of the store.","*BEEP.*","*Payment Approved.*","*Amount Processed: $37,850.00.*","Julian froze. All the color drained from his face as the receipt printer instantly began whirring, spitting out the long slip of paper.","He stared at the receipt. Then, he slowly looked up at Jude, who was leaning against the counter.","Jude had actually paid in full. Thirty-seven thousand dollars, swiped in a single second, without even a blink.","The other employees in the store exchanged shocked glances. The \"broke\" guy in the cheap suit actually had cash?","Despite the undeniable proof, Julian’s ego refused to let him back down. He swallowed hard, quickly regaining his sneer.","\"Well,\" Julian said, his voice dripping with venom as he handed the card back. \"Congratulations. You successfully bought a suit. I hope it was worth draining your entire life savings just to prove a point to a retail worker. Have fun eating instant noodles in your studio apartment for the next ten years.\"","The other two employees chuckled quietly from the corner.","It made sense. People did crazy, financially ruinous things when their pride was damaged.","Jude pulled out one of the chairs near the fitting rooms, sat down, and crossed his legs.","\"I have a business proposition,\" Jude said calmly. \"Go get your store manager.\"","Julian scowled. \"What are you talking about? You bought your suit. We’re done here. I’m not bothering my manager just because you want to complain about my attitude.\"","\"If you don’t bring him out here right now,\" Jude said, \"I will sit here until he walks the floor himself. And when he does, the consequences for you will be far worse than a simple complaint.\"","Before Julian could fire back another insult, the door to the back office swung open.","A sharply dressed man in his fifties stepped out, holding a tablet. He looked up and frowned. \"Julian? What is going on out here?\"","\"Manager Caldwell,\" Julian said quickly, stepping in front of Jude. \"This customer is causing a scene. He made a purchase, but now he’s refusing to leave and demanding to see you.\"","Caldwell sighed, pinching the bridge of his nose. He stepped around Julian to address the problematic customer directly.","\"Sir, I must ask you to—\"","Caldwell stopped dead in his tracks. His eyes widened behind his glasses, and his mouth fell open slightly.","\"Wait,\" Caldwell breathed. \"Is... is it you, sir?\"","Jude raised an eyebrow, genuinely surprised. \"Do we know each other?\"","Caldwell immediately tucked his tablet under his arm and sprinted forward, bowing at the waist.","\"Mr. Lawson!\" Caldwell said. \"What an absolute honor! I was having my morning espresso in the lobby of the Obsidian Grand two hours ago. I saw the General Manager himself carrying your breakfast tray to the private elevator! Anyone who commands that level of respect from the Obsidian is royalty in this district!\"","Julian’s jaw hit the floor. The Obsidian Grand? The General Manager acting as a *busboy* for this guy?","Jude smiled faintly. The system’s influence really did work in mysterious, convenient ways. \"Ah. You saw that, did you?\"","\"Yes, sir! My name is Caldwell. I run this flagship location,\" the manager said, sweating. \"Are you here to update your wardrobe?\"","\"I was,\" Jude said, leaning back in his chair and gesturing lazily toward Julian. \"In fact, I have a massive corporate acquisition coming up. I was planning to purchase this season’s entire catalogue for myself, and commission fifty bespoke suits for my new executive board.\"","Caldwell’s eyes practically turned into dollar signs.","That was a multi-million dollar transaction. It would make their quarterly quota in a single afternoon!","\"However,\" Jude continued, \"your stylist here just informed me that I look like a broke window-shopper, and suggested I spend the next ten years eating instant noodles. So, I’m thinking I might just take my business to the Italian boutique across the street.\""]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: The Customer Is Always Right","paragraphs":["\"What?\"","The two other employees standing near the cashmere display gasped audibly, their eyes darting between Jude and the manager.","Manager Caldwell remained perfectly still, though a bead of sweat formed at his temple.","He knew the elite clientele of the Zenith District well. For someone like this man to threaten to drop half a million dollars at a rival boutique... it wasn’t an empty threat.","Julian, however, was in denial. His face flushed angry crimson, and a frantic energy took over his posture.","\"Manager Caldwell, are you seriously listening to this guy?\" Julian protested, stepping forward and pointing a finger at Jude. \"He’s bluffing! He’s causing a scene just to stroke his own ego. Sure, he bought one suit, but I guarantee you that swiped the very last penny from whatever inheritance he stumbled into! He’s wasting our time. We should call security!\"","Manager Caldwell’s face contorted in horror. Was this stylist out of his mind?","\"Shut your mouth!\" Caldwell roared. \"Shut your mouth right this second and step away from him! Do you have any idea who you are speaking to?\"","Julian flinched, stepping back.","He had worked at Aurelius for three years and had never once seen the typically composed manager raise his voice, let alone scream...","\"But Manager, I—\"","\"I said quiet!\" Caldwell snarled. \"Did you leave your professional training at home today? Is this how we treat guests of the Obsidian Grand?\"","Julian crossed his arms. \"I’m just being realistic. Look at the guy. He’s trying to scare me, but I know a fraud when I see one. Half a million dollars? Yeah, right. He doesn’t have it.\"","Jude watched the meltdown with mild amusement.","He pulled his Platinum VIP Shopping Card from his pocket once again and set it flat on the glass display case.","\"Talk is cheap,\" Jude said, his voice unbothered. \"Actions aren’t. Manager Caldwell, I want fifty of your highest-tier bespoke suits, tailored to varying measurements which my assistant will provide later. Process the deposit right now.\"","Caldwell didn’t hesitate. He shoved Julian out of the way, scooped up the card with both hands, and rushed to the main terminal.","He punched in the transaction... a flat five hundred thousand dollars for the corporate reserve order.","He held his breath as the system processed.","*BEEP!*","*Payment Approved.*","When the long, detailed receipt began to print, the silence in the store was deafening. The other clerks felt their hearts drop into their stomachs.","He wasn’t bluffing. The guy in the cheap suit had just dropped over half a million dollars on a Tuesday morning.","Julian’s face went slack. The color drained from his cheeks, leaving him looking like a ghost.","His legs began to tremble as the gravity of his mistake finally crushed his ego. He had just horribly insulted a man who spent five hundred thousand dollars like it was pocket change!","Caldwell returned the card to Jude, bowing slightly. \"Your receipt, Mr. Lawson. And your card. Please, accept my deepest apologies for this unacceptable behavior.\"","\"Have the initial suit I bought tailored and sent to the Presidential Suite at the Obsidian,\" Jude said, sliding the card into his pocket. \"As for your employee... how you handle this will determine if I ever walk through those doors again.\"","It wasn’t an empty threat. Caldwell knew that a single negative word from a billionaire could ruin the boutique’s reputation among the city’s elite.","Caldwell spun around to face Julian, his eyes burning with fury. \"Your behavior is a disgrace to this establishment. You are fired. Furthermore, your commission for this month is forfeit. Pack your locker and get out of my store.\"","Julian looked like he was going to be sick.","Without a single word of protest, he lowered his head and shuffled toward the back room.","Caldwell shot a warning glare at the remaining employees, who dropped their gazes to the floor, terrified of meeting his eyes.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" Caldwell said, turning back with a strained smile. \"I assure you, this will never happen again. Is there anything else I can do for you today?\"","Jude nodded, satisfied with the outcome, and prepared to leave.","Just as he turned toward the entrance, the doors swung open, accompanied by a cheerful chime.","Two figures stepped into the boutique. The man wore a designer polo shirt and a flashy gold watch, while the woman clinging to his arm carried a handbag that cost more than most people’s annual rent.","It was Trent Belmont and Chloe...","Trent immediately spotted the manager and grinned, letting go of Chloe’s hand.","\"Caldwell, my man! Good to see you. I need some alterations done on the tux I bought last month.\"","Caldwell blinked, caught off guard by the sudden arrival of the Belmont heir.","But before the manager could greet him, Trent’s eyes swept across the room and landed on Jude.","Trent’s grin vanished, replaced by a look of disgust. \"What the hell is this?\"","Chloe gasped, covering her mouth as she recognized her ex-fiancé.","Then, a mocking laugh bubbled up from her throat.","\"Oh my god,\" Chloe sneered, stepping forward. \"Jude? What are you doing in a place like this? Did you get lost looking for the subway station? Or did you come in here to beg for a janitorial job since Sterling fired you yesterday?\"","Trent scoffed, looking at Caldwell. \"Caldwell, why is there a homeless guy standing in the middle of your showroom? Your security is slipping. Have him thrown out before he leaves a stench on the inventory.\"","Caldwell’s heart nearly stopped.","He looked back and forth between Jude and the Belmont heir, panic setting in.","Trent Belmont was a wealthy client, yes, but Jude had just demonstrated a level of liquid cash that was frankly terrifying.","\"Mr. Belmont,\" Caldwell said, abandoning his usual subservient tone. \"I must ask you to mind your words. Mr. Lawson is our most esteemed VIP client today.\"","Chloe let out a laugh. \"VIP? Him? Manager, you have to be joking. I lived with this loser. Until yesterday, he was a glorified car washer. I guarantee you he can’t even afford a pair of socks in this store. He’s probably trying to buy a tie on a five-year installment plan!\"","Caldwell’s expression darkened. \"Miss, I suggest you stop talking. Mr. Lawson just purchased a full bespoke vicuña suit in cash, and placed a reserve order for fifty more. He just finalized a transaction for over half a million dollars.\"","What?","Trent and Chloe completely froze. The arrogant smiles melted off their faces in an instant.","\"Half a million?\" Trent repeated, his voice cracking slightly.","He looked at Jude, then at the manager, waiting for the punchline. But Caldwell was deadly serious.","Chloe’s eyes widened to the size of saucers. She stared at Jude, her mind short-circuiting.","Over five hundred thousand dollars? In one morning? That was impossible.","He had exactly forty-two dollars in his account when she left him. How could he possibly drop half a million dollars on clothes?","\"Anyway, I have places to be,\" Jude said smoothly, ignoring the two statues standing near the door.","He didn’t even grant Chloe a second glance.","He walked right past them and stepped out into the bright sunlight.","Inside the boutique, Trent was still staring at the door, dumbfounded.","\"Caldwell... you’re lying. There is no way that guy has money. He’s a nobody!\"","Caldwell let out a sigh. \"Mr. Belmont, I personally watched him swipe a Platinum Elite card. Furthermore, I watched the General Manager of the Obsidian Grand Hotel personally serve him breakfast this morning. He is residing in their Presidential Suite.\"","Trent’s face lost all its color. He felt a sudden chill run down his spine.","The Obsidian Grand? The Belmont family owned a lot of real estate, but the Obsidian Grand was owned by a massive international conglomerate... a conglomerate that Trent’s father was currently begging for a partnership with.","If Jude was a top-tier VIP residing in the Presidential Suite, his influence was lightyears beyond what Trent could comprehend.","And Trent had just publicly humiliated him. Twice!","\"Oh my god,\" Trent muttered, panic seizing his chest.","If his father found out he had offended a hidden billionaire connected to the Obsidian... he would be disowned before sunset!","\"Wait!\" Trent shouted, shoving past Chloe and sprinting out the doors onto the sidewalk.","Chloe stood alone in the center of the boutique, her hands trembling.","She looked at the receipt still sitting on the manager’s counter, the numbers mocking her decisions.","Jude was standing near the curb, waiting for a luxury town car to pull around.","\"Jude! Wait! Mr. Lawson, please wait!\" Trent yelled, sprinting down the sidewalk."]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: Live for the Audience","paragraphs":["Trent nearly tripped over his own expensive loafers as he skidded to a halt a few feet away from Jude.","If his father found out he had openly mocked a top-tier VIP residing in the Obsidian Grand’s Presidential Suite, the Belmont family would cut him off before dinner.","He needed to fix this, and he needed to fix it right now.","\"Mr. Lawson, please,\" Trent gasped, reaching into his blazer pocket.","He pulled out a customized, gold-plated cigar case and flipped it open with trembling fingers, extending it outward.","\"I... I was completely out of line back there. I didn’t know who you were. Please, have a Cuban. On me. Let me make this right.\"","Jude looked at the heir, then down at the expensive cigars.","A day ago, a guy like Trent wouldn’t have even looked in Jude’s direction unless it was to demand he wash his tires. Now, he was bowing like a frightened servant.","\"I don’t smoke,\" Jude said flatly, not making a single move to take the offering.","Trent awkwardly retracted the case. \"Right. Of course. N-Not smoking is the way to go. Health is wealth, right? Haha...\"","Chloe came rushing out of the boutique, her face flushed red.","\"Jude, you need to tell me what is going on right now,\" Chloe demanded. \"Were you lying to me this whole time? Were you hiding money from me? Is this some kind of sick test?\"","Jude looked at her, his expression detached. He felt absolutely nothing. The heartbreak that had consumed him yesterday was entirely gone, replaced by an untouchable calm.","\"I didn’t lie to you, Chloe,\" Jude said mildly. \"I was exactly as broke as you thought I was yesterday.\"","Chloe’s eyes darted frantically. \"Then how? How did you just drop half a million dollars? How are you staying at the Obsidian?\"","\"Things change,\" Jude replied, checking his watch. \"I realized my potential was being wasted scrubbing rims. In fact, I’m putting together the capital to purchase a controlling stake in Zenith Motors by the end of the month.\"","Chloe felt like all the oxygen had been sucked out of the air.","Buy Zenith Motors? The high-end dealership where they had both worked? The dealership where the general manager had fired him yesterday?","The scale of the social leap Jude was describing was incomprehensible.","A sleek, black Maybach town car pulled up to the curb. The driver stepped out and opened the rear door for Jude, bowing respectfully.","Jude didn’t say another word. He stepped into the plush interior.","Chloe stood frozen on the pavement, watching the taillights disappear.","The regret in her gut was so intense it made her nauseous.","She slowly turned to Trent, reaching out to grab his arm for comfort. \"Trent, I—\"","Trent slapped her hand away.","\"Don’t touch me,\" Trent hissed, his eyes wide. \"You told me he was a nobody! You made me insult a man who could probably buy my father’s company and liquidate it for fun!\"","\"I didn’t know!\" Chloe cried, tears welling in her eyes. \"You heard him, he was broke yesterday! And you’re the one who called him trash!\"","\"Because you set him up as a joke!\" Trent roared, running a hand through his hair. \"If my family loses the Obsidian contract over this, my father will destroy me. And I swear, I will destroy you.\"","Without waiting for a response, Trent turned on his heel and stormed down the avenue, pulling his phone out to call his crisis management team.","Chloe was left standing alone on the sidewalk, the bags of her recent shopping spree suddenly feeling like lead weights.","She had tried to trade up. Instead, she had lost everything...","***","The ride in the Maybach was smooth. Jude drafted a text to the concierge desk at the Obsidian Grand, instructing them to receive the shipment of bespoke suits from Aurelius and hang them in his suite’s master closet.","The concierge replied in less than thirty seconds: *Consider it done, Mr. Lawson. Shall we prepare a light lunch for your return?*","Jude smiled, typing back a quick refusal.","He had the driver drop him off near the Sapphire Promenade, an upscale outdoor plaza lined with artisan cafes, high-end boutiques, and beautiful fountains.","The weather was perfect, and Jude just wanted to enjoy the simple pleasure of walking around without the crushing anxiety of checking his bank balance every five minutes.","He grabbed an iced coffee from a nearby artisan stand and leaned against a railing near the central fountain, watching the crowds of people walk by.","Just a few yards away, a young woman was holding a phone attached to a gimbal, speaking animatedly into the camera.","She was dressed in a provocative outfit... a cropped top that left little to the imagination, and a tight skirt.","Her name was Lexi, and she was a live streamer known for \"loyalty tests.\"","\"Alright, chat, do I look good?\" Lexi whispered into her microphone, giggling as the comments on her screen flew by at lightspeed. \"Today we’re playing a fun little game. We are going to find a guy who is out with his girlfriend, and I’m going to pretend to faint. Let’s see if these so-called ’loyal’ boyfriends can resist catching me. Nothing like a little drama to spice up a Tuesday afternoon, right?\"","The internet loved trainwrecks, and Lexi’s viewer count was rapidly climbing.","She scanned the plaza, her eyes darting around like a hawk looking for prey.","She quickly locked onto a young, ordinary-looking couple walking near the fountain. The guy was wearing a graphic t-shirt and glasses, and his girlfriend was holding onto his arm, chatting happily about a movie.","Lexi smirked.","She adjusted her top to make it sit a little lower, took a deep breath, and walked directly into their path.","As she passed the boyfriend, Lexi let out a dramatic, breathy gasp and suddenly collapsed sideways, throwing her weight against the guy’s chest.","\"Oh!\" the glasses-wearing guy yelped, dropping his shopping bag to catch her.","Lexi slumped against him.","She looked up at him through her lashes, ensuring he had a view down her top.","\"I’m so, so sorry,\" Lexi murmured in a sickeningly sweet voice. \"I just got so dizzy all of a sudden. I think my blood sugar is low. Could you maybe hold me for a second?\"","The guy’s face turned bright red. He stammered. \"U-Uh, yeah. Sure. Are you okay? Do you need to sit down?\"","His girlfriend, standing right next to him, looked like she was about to explode.","\"Excuse me!\" the girlfriend snapped, grabbing her boyfriend’s shoulder. \"She can sit on the bench! You don’t need to hold her like that! Let go of her!\"","The guy stepped back, looking incredibly guilty, which only made his girlfriend angrier.","\"Are you serious right now?\" she yelled. \"You’re drooling over her! I told you I wanted to go to the jewelry store earlier and you said we were in a rush, but you have time to hold a random girl in the middle of the street?\"","\"Babe, she was falling,\" the guy pleaded, sweating. \"I was just helping.\"","\"If you want me to believe that, you can buy me that necklace I asked for right now!\" the girlfriend demanded, crossing her arms.","\"The necklace is two grand!\" the guy cried.","\"Then I guess we’re done!\"","As the couple devolved into a screaming match, eventually storming off toward the jewelry stores, Lexi stepped back into the shadows and laughed quietly into her microphone.","\"Oh my god, chat, did you see that?\" Lexi giggled, watching a flurry of donations pop up on her screen.","\"They are literally about to break up over a simple stumble. Men are so easy. Thank you for the fifty dollars, User99!\"","Lexi flipped her hair over her shoulder, thrilled by the spike in her engagement metrics.","\"Okay, that was fun, but let’s up the stakes. Let’s find someone with some actual money. If I can get a rich guy to embarrass himself on stream, we’ll go viral for sure.\"","Lexi turned her camera toward the plaza entrance, scanning the crowd.","Her eyes suddenly locked onto Jude.","He was leaning against the railing, casually sipping his coffee. But what caught Lexi’s eye wasn’t Jude himself... it was the imposing Maybach town car parked at the curb behind him, and the uniformed driver who was respectfully waiting near the door for him.","Lexi’s eyes lit up with excitement. *Jackpot.*"]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: Caught in 4K","paragraphs":["\"Look at this guy,\" Lexi whispered to her phone, ensuring the camera had a clear angle of Jude and the Maybach. \"He’s got the whole brooding, mysterious billionaire vibe going on. But a pretty face and a fancy ride mean nothing to me. Watch me wrap this guy around my little finger.\"","Lexi smoothed out her skirt, put on her best damsel-in-distress expression, and walked toward Jude.","Just as she passed him, she let out a delicate gasp, intentionally rolling her ankle.","She threw her weight sideways, aiming to crash directly into his chest.","*Got him,* she thought, preparing for the inevitable awkward grab and the flustered apologies.","The five attribute points he had allocated into Strength and Agility fired instantly. Instead of fumbling or stepping back, Jude smoothly shifted his stance.","He didn’t just brace her fall; he caught her completely, wrapping one strong arm around her waist and the other under her knees, lifting her off the ground before her shoes even scuffed the pavement.","Lexi’s breath hitched. She found herself suddenly cradled against his chest, staring up at him in genuine shock.","\"Oh,\" Lexi stammered, forgetting her script. \"I... my blood sugar... I’m so dizzy.\"","\"Is that so?\" Jude asked.","He glanced at the gimbal clutched in her right hand, the red recording light blinking steadily.","Without breaking a sweat, Jude walked three steps to a bench and deposited her neatly onto it.","\"Dizziness is dangerous. Luckily, you bumped into me,\" Jude said, a smirk playing on his lips.","Lexi was speechless. *What is he doing?*","Jude turned to the small artisan kiosk right next to the bench, tossed a crinkled two-dollar bill onto the counter, and grabbed a water bottle.","He twisted the cap off and handed it to Lexi.","\"Here,\" Jude said, patting her gently on the shoulder. \"Hydrate. It would be a real shame if you actually passed out and your viewers missed the rest of your broadcast.\"","Lexi’s jaw dropped.","With a nod, Jude turned and continued his walk down the promenade.","Lexi looked down at her phone screen. The chat was moving so fast it was a blur of text and emojis.","*LMAOOO HE READ HER LIKE A BOOK!*","*Alpha energy.*","*He gave her a $2 water and left!*","*Streamer taking massive Ls today!*","The guy with the glasses, who was still standing outside the jewelry store across the plaza after blowing two thousand dollars to appease his angry girlfriend, watched the entire interaction.","He looked at Jude, who had defused a manipulative trap with a cheap bottle of water and a smirk, and then looked at his own empty wallet.","A wave of profound depression washed over him.","Lexi’s face burned hot with embarrassment. Her smile shattered.","*Dammit!* she thought, her knuckles turning white as she gripped her phone.","Her grand plan to embarrass a rich guy had backfired. Jude hadn’t looked like a creep; he looked cool, and he had made her look like an amateur.","\"No way,\" Lexi muttered under her breath, glaring at Jude’s retreating back. \"I am not letting this go. I’m going to expose him. Look at that cheap suit he’s wearing! He’s probably just a chauffeur posing in front of his boss’s car!\"","Ignoring her chat’s teasing, Lexi stood up and began tailing Jude from a distance.","A few blocks away, Jude’s phone buzzed in his pocket. It was a message from Manager Caldwell at the Aurelius boutique.","*Mr. Lawson, the reserve order of fifty bespoke suits has been fully prepped. We have loaded it into our private transport truck. However, store policy requires a signature for any release exceeding $250,000. We are parked just at the edge of the Zenith District.*","Jude tapped out a quick confirmation. He wasn’t far. He adjusted his collar and walked toward the designated intersection.","At the corner of the high-end district, a black transport truck was idling with its hazard lights blinking.","Pedestrians were giving it curious looks. Usually, trucks that size were reserved for moving entire store inventories.","Jude approached the corner, looking for Caldwell.","Suddenly, Lexi popped out from behind a nearby pillar, a sickly-sweet smile plastered on her face.","\"Wow, what a coincidence!\" Lexi exclaimed, shoving her camera slightly in his direction. \"We meet again! I didn’t get to properly thank you for the water earlier.\"","Jude stopped, letting out a sigh. This woman was remarkably persistent. \"Don’t mention it. Feeling better?\"","\"Much better,\" Lexi said, her eyes doing a slow sweep of his faded, off-the-rack polyester suit. \"Though I have to ask... what brings you to the Zenith District? This is the most expensive street in the city. You aren’t planning on buying anything, are you?\"","She was openly mocking him now, trying to salvage her ego by pointing out his cheap clothes to her audience.","Jude didn’t care about the stream, but her assumptions were getting tiresome.","\"No,\" Jude said simply. \"I’m not here to buy anything right now.\"","Lexi’s eyes lit up in triumph. *I knew it. He’s completely broke.*","At that exact moment, a man in a flashy silk shirt and a diamond-encrusted watch strutted out of a nearby luxury jewelry store, a young model hanging off his arm. He reeked of new money and arrogance.","Lexi immediately saw an opportunity to double down. She turned her camera to the flashy man.","\"Excuse me, sir! I’m doing a quick lifestyle interview,\" Lexi said cheerfully. \"Would you mind sharing what you just bought for this lovely lady?\"","The flashy man puffed out his chest, thrilled to have an audience.","\"Oh, nothing major. Just a thirty-thousand-dollar diamond tennis bracelet for my baby here. The markets have been good to me, so what’s thirty grand, right?\"","\"Wow!\" Lexi gasped. \"That is incredible! A real high-roller. What do you think about people who come to the Zenith District just to window shop because they can’t afford a single item?\"","She angled the camera directly at Jude as she asked the question.","The flashy man looked Jude up and down, taking in the frayed lapels and the scuffed shoes.","He let out a snort.","\"Look at him,\" the man laughed. \"It’s pathetic. Guys like this just come here to stare at things they’ll never touch. With a suit like that, he’s probably a lost intern or someone’s driver. Frankly, the security shouldn’t even let people dressed like that onto this street.\"","The model on his arm giggled loudly. \"So true, babe. Good thing you aren’t a broke loser.\"","Lexi was ecstatic. She had successfully flipped the narrative. She turned back to Jude, offering a mock-sympathetic pout.","\"Aw, don’t feel bad, handsome! Maybe one day you’ll save up enough to buy a nice tie!\"","Before Jude could even open his mouth to reply, a voice echoed down the street.","\"Mr. Lawson! Mr. Lawson, I am so sorry for the wait!\"","Manager Caldwell, flanked by three identically dressed boutique employees holding clipboards, came sprinting out of the Aurelius storefront.","He looked frantic, ignoring Lexi and the flashy man as he skidded to a halt in front of Jude and bowed deeply.","\"We had to secure the transport properly,\" Caldwell breathed, offering Jude a stack of invoices. \"Please, sir, your signature.\"","Jude took the pen and signed the top sheet.","\"Excellent! Open it up, boys!\" Caldwell shouted.","The employees rushed to the back of the black transport truck and hit the hydraulic lift.","The doors rolled up, revealing the interior.","The truck was packed front-to-back with dozens of premium garment bags, all bearing the golden *Aurelius* crest.","There were rows of bespoke suits, luxury outerwear, and perfectly packaged dress shoes.","The flashy man stopped laughing. His jaw dropped.","\"Is this everything?\" Jude asked, handing the clipboard back.","\"Yes, Mr. Lawson!\" Caldwell announced proudly, loud enough for the entire street to hear. \"Fifty bespoke corporate suits, plus your entire personal seasonal wardrobe buyout! A fully paid transaction of five hundred and thirty-seven thousand dollars! We are ready to transport it to your suite at the Obsidian Grand whenever you say the word!\"","The flashy man’s eyes rolled back in his head.","Over half a million dollars? On *clothes*?"]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: The Viral Stream","paragraphs":["Employees from Aurelius were organizing the garment bags inside the truck.","It was a bustling scene that had pedestrian traffic grinding to an absolute halt. People were pulling out their phones, whispering and pointing at the sheer volume of luxury goods being loaded for a single individual.","\"Wait a moment,\" Jude called out, stepping closer to the hydraulic lift.","He pointed to a velvet-lined lockbox resting on one of the transport trolleys. \"Let me see that.\"","\"Of course, Mr. Lawson,\" Caldwell said, rushing forward to unlock the small case with a specialized key.","He popped the lid open, revealing the single accessory Jude had requested to cap off his order.","It was a platinum Audemars Piguet Royal Oak, encrusted with subtle diamonds along the bezel.","The onlookers gasped, a collective murmur of shock rippling through the crowd.","Anyone with even a passing knowledge of horology knew that specific timepiece retailed for over $250,000 on the secondary market!","Jude lifted the metal from the cushion. He didn’t ask for Caldwell to size it; he simply slipped it onto his wrist and clamped the clasp shut. It fit perfectly.","He wasn’t usually one to care about flashy accessories. But after dealing with Trent, the snobby stylist Julian, and now this obnoxious streamer, he realized something fundamental about the ultra-wealthy.","With this Audemars Piguet on his wrist, nobody would ever mistake him for a lost intern or a chauffeur ever again.","It was the ultimate deterrent against the world’s endless supply of arrogant fools.","\"Perfect,\" Jude said, nodding in satisfaction. \"It’s a beautiful piece.\"","Standing a few feet away, Lexi felt like her soul was leaving her body.","She stared at the watch. She stared at the hundreds of thousands of dollars in bespoke clothing. Then, she remembered how she had literally thrown herself into this man’s arms just twenty minutes ago, hoping to embarrass him.","He hadn’t just rejected her; he had bought her a two-dollar plastic water bottle and treated her like a confused child.","The regret hit Lexi so hard she almost felt ill. She was looking at a man who could likely buy her streaming platform, and she had spent the entire afternoon mocking him for wearing a polyester suit.","*If I hadn’t acted like such a manipulative brat,* Lexi screamed, her fingernails biting into her palms, *I could have actually gotten his number!*","The flashy man standing next to her had gone silent. He worked in finance, and he could do the math.","A man who casually drops over half a million dollars on *clothes*, and another quarter of a million on a watch to match, doesn’t just have a few million in the bank.","That kind of liquid, careless spending was exclusively reserved for titans.","He realized with sudden clarity that if he had pushed his insults just a fraction further, Jude could likely have his entire investment firm liquidated by Friday...","He lowered his head, turned around, and sprinted away into the crowd, desperate to disappear before Jude decided to remember his face.","Jude ignored them both. He offered Caldwell a nod. \"Take it all to the Obsidian. My driver is waiting.\"","\"Right away, sir!\" Caldwell bowed.","Lexi remained frozen as Jude walked past her and slid into the backseat of the waiting Maybach town car. The door clicked shut, and the vehicle glided into the afternoon traffic.","Lexi stood on the pavement, her mouth opening and closing like a stranded fish.","She finally looked down at her phone screen, which was overheating from the sheer volume of chat messages flooding the server.","Her live-stream had exploded.","*BRO BOUGHT A TRUCK FULL OF CLOTHES!!*","*Half a million?! Who is that guy?!*","*He really gave her a $2 water and then went to pick up a $250k watch I am CRYING.*","*Lexi fumbled the biggest bag in human history.*","The viewer count in her room had skyrocketed from 3,000 to over 50,000 in less than 5 minutes!","People were screen-recording the broadcast, clipping the exact moment Jude caught her, dropped her on the bench, and handed her the water bottle.","They combined it with the footage of the transport truck and the platinum watch.","Within two hours, the footage would cross platforms, algorithmically pushed to millions of feeds!","*#WaterBottleBillionaire*","*#ZenithDistrictFlex*","*#LexiFumblesTheBag*","The internet was obsessed. Users were trying to identify the handsome man in the cheap suit who commanded such absurd wealth.","Men praised his stoic, alpha demeanor in the face of a manipulative streamer, while women flooded comment sections swooning over the way he carried her before coldly walking away.","Jude, who rarely used social media even before his life flipped upside down, was oblivious to his skyrocketing internet fame.","He arrived back at the Obsidian Grand Hotel in peace.","By the time he stepped out of his private elevator and into the Presidential Suite, the hotel’s elite housekeeping staff had already unloaded the transport truck.","Jude walked into the master bedroom and opened the walk-in closet.","It was fully stocked. Rows of perfectly tailored bespoke suits, cashmere sweaters, silk dress shirts, and imported leather shoes lined the illuminated racks.","It looked like a high-end boutique had been teleported directly into his room.","Jude took off his cheap, wrinkled polyester jacket and dropped it into the trash can.","He changed into a set of incredibly soft, charcoal-grey designer loungewear.","The system’s attribute points had broadened his shoulders and tightened his core, making the designer clothes look like they had been sculpted directly onto him.","He walked over to the floor-to-ceiling window, pouring himself a glass of sparkling water from the minibar.","Jude took a sip, his mind already calculating his next move.","Now, it was time to put his plan into motion.","He had told Chloe he was going to purchase a controlling stake in Zenith Motors, and he hadn’t been bluffing.","He wanted to see the look on General Manager Sterling’s face when Jude walked through the dealership doors not as an employee, but as the owner. He was just about to open his laptop to research corporate acquisition firms when his phone suddenly vibrated on the countertop...","Jude picked it up, expecting a message from the hotel concierge or perhaps an alert from his banking app.","Instead, an unknown, out-of-state number was flashing on the screen.","Jude narrowed his eyes, answering the call and raising the phone to his ear. \"Hello?\"","\"Is this Jude Lawson?\" a professional woman’s voice asked on the other end of the line.","\"It is. Who is calling?\"","\"My name is Victoria,\" the woman replied. \"I am a Senior Partner at Vance & Sterling Mergers and Acquisitions. I understand you have recently come into a substantial amount of capital, Mr. Lawson, and I believe we have a lucrative conversation ahead of us.\""]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: Who Is the New Owner?","paragraphs":["Jude leaned against the counter, a smile touching his lips. \"Word travels fast in this city. Who gave you my number?\"","\"In my line of work, Mr. Lawson, information is the most valuable currency,\" Victoria said. \"When the General Manager of the Obsidian Grand personally clears the Presidential Suite for a new resident who subsequently drops half a million dollars at a local boutique, flags are raised on every major financial radar. I represent clients who specialize in aggressive corporate takeovers. If you are looking to invest your new capital, I can facilitate the acquisition of virtually any asset in the district.\"","\"Any asset?\" Jude asked, his eyes drifting toward the skyline outside his window.","\"Name it.\"","\"Zenith Motors,\" Jude said flatly. \"The flagship dealership downtown. I want a controlling stake, and I want it expedited.\"","There was a brief pause on the line, followed by the sound of rapid typing.","\"Zenith Motors,\" Victoria mused. \"Their parent company has been severely over-leveraged for the past two quarters. The current owner is bleeding cash trying to keep their inventory afloat. It won’t be cheap, but a hostile buyout is entirely feasible if you have the liquid capital. I can have a preliminary dossier and transfer contracts drawn up by tomorrow morning.\"","\"Have them ready,\" Jude said. \"Meet me in the lobby of the Obsidian Grand at nine.\"","He hung up the phone, a sense of satisfaction settling in his chest.","Needing a change of scenery from his massive suite, Jude decided to head down to the hotel’s exclusive VIP lounge for a drink.","He slipped on his new Audemars Piguet watch and took the private elevator down to the ground floor.","The lounge was dimly lit, reeking of old money, expensive cigars, and aged scotch.","Jude took a seat at the bar.","The bartender, a sharply dressed man in his thirties, immediately walked over.","He poured a glass of premium whiskey on the rocks and slid it toward Jude, looking incredibly nervous.","\"On the house, Mr. Lawson,\" the bartender said. \"Though, if I may be so bold... are you aware that you’ve broken the internet tonight?\"","Jude paused, the glass halfway to his mouth. \"Excuse me?\"","The bartender pulled a tablet from beneath the counter and turned the screen around.","Jude stared at the display.","It was a live feed of the city’s top trending topics across three different social media platforms.","*#WaterBottleBillionaire*","*#ZenithDistrictFlex*","*#AureliusBuyout*","*#RichestManInACheapSuit*","Every single top trend was accompanied by crystal-clear video clips.","There was footage of Jude catching the streamer Lexi, depositing her on the bench, and handing her a two-dollar water bottle.","Below that, there was a viral clip of the transport truck outside the boutique, with Caldwell screaming about a $500,000 transaction.","The comments were a unified wall of awe.","\"Bro dropped half a mil on clothes and rejected an influencer with a plastic bottle. Legendary.\"","\"Who is this guy?!\"","\"The way the flashy guy ran away was hilarious! The WaterBottleBillionaire is him!\"","Jude let out a long sigh. He had never asked for the spotlight, let alone internet fame.","He rubbed his temples. \"I’d appreciate it if hotel security kept any vloggers or paparazzi off the premises.\"","\"Already taken care of, sir. We’ve doubled the perimeter guard,\" the bartender assured him.","Jude took a sip of his whiskey, glancing away from the screen.","As he looked into the reflection of the mirror behind the bar, a familiar face caught his attention.","Sitting in a secluded booth in the darkest corner of the lounge was Trent Belmont.","However, Trent didn’t look like the arrogant heir who had strutted through the car dealership yesterday. He looked pale, sickly, and terrified.","Sitting across from him was an older, fiercely intimidating man with silver hair... Arthur Belmont, the head of the Belmont real estate empire.","Jude subtly adjusted his position to listen.","\"You absolute idiot,\" Arthur hissed, slamming his fist quietly onto the table. \"Do you have any idea what you’ve done? The Obsidian conglomerate is reviewing our contract for the new commercial district tomorrow. And I just get a call from a boutique manager telling me my son publicly humiliated their top VIP?\"","Trent flinched, shrinking into the booth.","\"Dad, I swear, I didn’t know! He was wearing garbage! I thought he was a nobody!\"","\"You don’t think!\" Arthur snarled. \"We are hanging by a thread with this deal. If this VIP decides to mention your little stunt to the conglomerate’s board, we are finished. What is his name? I need to send an apology gift immediately.\"","Trent swallowed hard. He was entirely too cowardly to admit to his father that the ’ultra-VIP’ was the exact same dealership employee that Trent had bragged about getting fired yesterday.","\"I... I didn’t catch his name,\" Trent lied.","Jude smirked into his glass. He snapped a quick mental picture of Trent’s miserable state.","Pulling out his phone, Jude navigated to his contacts and found the name of the only person at Zenith Motors who had ever treated him with basic human decency: Maya, the inventory manager.","Jude quickly typed out a message.","*Maya. Make sure you are on the showroom floor tomorrow at 10:00 AM. Don’t take an early lunch.*","A few seconds later, his phone buzzed with a reply.","*Jude? What are you talking about? You got fired! Sterling said he’d call the cops if you ever set foot on the property again. Please don’t do anything crazy!*","Jude chuckled, typing his response.","*Just trust me. Tomorrow, everything changes.*","He locked his phone and finished his drink, thoroughly looking forward to the morning.","***","Meanwhile, across the city, the lights were still blazing inside the managerial office of Zenith Motors. General Manager Sterling was pacing back and forth behind his desk.","He had just received a phone call from the regional owner of the dealership.","\"A total buyout,\" Sterling muttered to himself, rubbing his palms together. \"A mysterious billionaire is coming to evaluate the dealership for a total buyout tomorrow morning.\"","Sterling couldn’t believe his luck...","The dealership had been struggling, and Sterling had been terrified of losing his job if they filed for bankruptcy.","But if a billionaire was swooping in to buy the place? This was his golden ticket.","If he rolled out the red carpet and impressed this mysterious tycoon, the new owner would undoubtedly promote him to a regional Vice President position!","\"This is it,\" Sterling whispered. \"My big break.\"","He stormed out of his office, stepping out onto the showroom floor where the night crew was finishing their inventory checks.","Maya was standing near the front desk, looking at her phone with a confused expression.","\"Listen up, everyone!\" Sterling barked, clapping his hands together. \"Tomorrow morning is the most important day in the history of this dealership! We have a VIP buyer arriving. I want this floor immaculate! I want the cars polished until they blind me! If anyone messes this up, I will fire you on the spot, just like I did to that worthless trash Jude yesterday!\"","Maya frowned, looking from the manager back down to the cryptic text message on her screen.","\"Do you hear me?\" Sterling yelled, pointing a finger at the staff. \"The new owner is coming!\""]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Blind Faith","paragraphs":["Inside the penthouse boardroom of Belmont Enterprises, Arthur Belmont stood at the head of a table, his gaze sweeping over his top executives.","Trent sat near the middle of the table, looking exhausted, nursing a cup of coffee.","\"The Obsidian Conglomerate has yet to respond to my inquiries this morning,\" Arthur said. \"If we do not secure the commercial district contract with them by Friday, our stock is going to take a catastrophic hit. I want every available resource dedicated to finding out the identity of the VIP staying in their Presidential Suite. If we can appease him, we save the deal.\"","The executives nodded.","\"Sir, forgive the interruption,\" a junior executive at the far end of the table said, timidly raising a tablet. \"But speaking of the Zenith District... have you seen the trending footage from yesterday afternoon? It’s dominating every major social feed.\"","Arthur frowned, clearly annoyed by the distraction. \"I do not care about social media trends, Marcus.\"","\"I understand, sir, but the footage involves the Obsidian Grand, and a transaction of over $500,000,\" Marcus explained, quickly casting the video from his tablet onto the projector screen at the front of the boardroom.","The video began to play.","It was the viral clip of Jude catching the streamer Lexi, shutting her down with the $2 water bottle, and then panning to Manager Caldwell announcing the staggering $537,000 wardrobe buyout.","Trent dropped his coffee cup.","\"That’s him!\" Trent shouted, shooting up from his chair.","His face drained of color as he pointed a shaking finger at the screen.","\"Dad, that’s the guy! That’s Jude! The broke loser from the dealership!\"","Arthur’s eyes narrowed as he stepped closer to the projector, scrutinizing the man in the video. \"This is the man you insulted? The one you claimed was a penniless car washer?\"","\"Yes! But look at the video!\" Trent panicked. \"He just dropped half a million dollars in cash! He really is a billionaire!\"","Arthur stared at the frozen frame of Jude signing the clipboard. He looked at Jude’s faded, poorly fitting polyester suit.","Then, a smirk spread across the older man’s face.","Arthur let out a laugh.","\"Are you really this gullible, Trent?\" Arthur asked, shaking his head. \"Look at the production quality. Look at the camera angles. You actually believe a centimillionaire walks around in a suit that looks like it was pulled from a dumpster?\"","Trent blinked, confused. \"But... the manager...\"","\"It is a viral marketing stunt,\" Arthur stated, waving his hand at the screen. \"Aurelius is a high-end brand. They clearly orchestrated this ’hidden billionaire’ narrative to boost their online engagement with the younger demographic. This Jude character is nothing more than a struggling actor they hired off the street to play a role.\"","The executives in the room immediately relaxed.","\"Ah, classic guerrilla marketing,\" the Chief Financial Officer noted with a smirk. \"It’s actually quite brilliant. Frame the ’rich guy’ in cheap clothes to create a viral contrast.\"","\"Exactly,\" Arthur agreed, turning away from the screen. \"It’s all fake. A perfectly staged scene for the internet. Trent, I can’t believe you let a paid actor terrify you like this.\"","Trent felt a wave of relief wash over him. His father was right... It made perfect sense.","Jude didn’t have any money; he had just stumbled into a gig as a brand ambassador for a viral video.","\"I... I guess I panicked,\" Trent laughed nervously, sitting back down. \"So he really is just a broke loser.\"","Arthur sighed, taking his seat at the head of the table. \"Forget the actor. Now, if the Obsidian deal completely stalls, we have a secondary safety net. I have been in talks with the parent company of Zenith Motors. They are planning a multi-million-dollar expansion of their dealership lots across the state. If we secure the real estate provisioning for that expansion, we can offset our current quarterly losses entirely.\"","The executives murmured in agreement, unaware that the very dealership they were banking their entire corporate survival on was currently changing hands.","...","Miles away, the morning sun was reflecting off the hood of a sleek, black Maybach town car as it cruised down the bustling city streets.","Jude sat in the spacious rear cabin, looking out the windows.","He was wearing one of his newly delivered bespoke suits.","Sitting across from him was Victoria. The Senior Partner looked incredibly sharp in a white designer blazer, a folder resting in her lap.","\"The hostile takeover was successful, Mr. Lawson,\" Victoria said, tapping the folder with a manicured fingernail. \"By leveraging your liquid capital through our shell entities, we bypassed the board’s usual waiting periods. You now hold 78% of the parent company’s voting shares. The ink dried at 7:00 this morning. Zenith Motors is officially yours.\"","\"Excellent work, Victoria,\" Jude said.","\"I must admit, Mr. Lawson, this is unusual,\" Victoria noted, a curious glint in her eye. \"Most of my clients who execute takeovers of this magnitude prefer to stay in the shadows, or at least wait a few weeks before making their presence known. Showing up to a mid-level dealership in person at nine in the morning on the very day of the acquisition... it’s incredibly aggressive.\"","Jude offered a smile. \"I’m a hands-on owner. Besides, I left something behind yesterday.\"","Victoria chuckled, adjusting her glasses. \"Well, their General Manager, a Mr. Sterling, was informed late last night that the new majority shareholder would be conducting a surprise inspection today. He has been hyperventilating on the phone to my assistants all morning.\"","\"Good,\" Jude said, his eyes darkening slightly.","The Maybach turned off the main avenue, its tires gliding onto the freshly paved VIP entrance of Zenith Motors.","Through the glass, Jude could see the entire scene perfectly...","General Manager Sterling was standing at the absolute front of the red-carpeted entryway, wearing his best suit, sweating despite the cool morning air.","Behind him, lined up with military precision, were the sales associates, the finance team, and the inventory staff.","Maya was standing near the back, looking nervous and confused.","Derek, the junior associate who had offered Jude the $20 bill, was standing near the front, trying to look incredibly professional.","They were all holding their breath, waiting for the mysterious billionaire who held their careers in the palm of his hand to step out of the car.","The Maybach rolled to a silent stop right in front of the doors.","The uniformed driver immediately stepped out and jogged around the rear of the vehicle.","Sterling quickly wiped his palms on his trousers, slapping on a smile as the driver reached for the door handle.","*Here we go,* Sterling thought. *Time to meet the boss.*"]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: Buying Zenith Motors","paragraphs":["The door swung open.","A shoe stepped onto the pavement. Then, a man emerged.","Sterling immediately bowed at the waist, his rehearsed greeting tumbling out of his mouth.","\"Welcome to Zenith Motors, sir! It is our absolute honor to host you today. I am General Manager Sterling, and I—\"","Sterling looked up to make eye contact.","The words died in his throat.","The smile froze on his face, decaying into an expression of sheer horror.","His eyes bugged out so far they looked like they were going to pop out of his skull.","Standing behind Sterling, Derek dropped his inventory clipboard.","Maya covered her mouth with both hands, a gasp escaping her lips.","Jude casually buttoned the center button of his blazer and offered Sterling a faint smile. \"Good morning, Sterling. The showroom looks a bit dusty. Did you clean the glass in the back like I asked?\"","Sterling’s brain short-circuited. He looked at the hyper-luxury Maybach, then at the watch, and finally back to Jude’s face.","\"J-Jude?!\" Sterling shrieked, his voice cracking. \"What the hell are you doing?! Did you steal that car? Get off this lot right now before I call the police!\"","Before Jude could even respond, Victoria Vance stepped out of the Maybach. She adjusted her designer glasses, clutching a folder to her chest.","\"I would strongly advise against that, Mr. Sterling,\" Victoria said. \"Calling the authorities on the majority owner of this establishment would constitute a severe breach of your employment contract.\"","Sterling stumbled back. \"Owner?! Are you insane? This man is a fraud! He was washing tires and serving coffee here! I fired him myself! He has zero money!\"","Victoria opened the folder and presented the first page. \"As of seven o’clock this morning, Mr. Jude Lawson successfully acquired seventy-eight percent of the voting shares of Zenith Motors’ parent company via a direct wire transfer. The ink is dry. The board has signed off. This dealership, the inventory, the land, and your employment contract, now belong entirely to him.\"","The staff gasped.","Derek looked like he was going to pass out. He had offered this man a crumpled twenty-dollar bill!","He had told him to buy a bus ticket... Now, Jude had literally returned to buy the entire multi-million-dollar facility out from under them.","Jude didn’t wait for Sterling to recover from his collapse. He simply walked past the manager, pushing through the doors into the main showroom.","Jude walked to the center of the showroom floor, stopping in front of the elevated rotating display.","Resting on the platform was the newly imported Zenith V12 hypercar. The $3,000,000 vehicle Chloe had mockingly told him to buy just twenty-four hours ago.","Jude admired the sleek curves of the car. It really was a masterpiece of engineering.","\"Victoria,\" Jude said, not looking away from the car. \"Have the transport team load this V12 up. I want it shipped to the private garage at the Obsidian Grand. I’ve been meaning to pick up a weekend car.\"","\"Right away, Mr. Lawson,\" Victoria noted, pulling out her phone.","Sterling, finally regaining control of his legs, came sprinting into the showroom. His face was a mask of panic. The realization that the billionaire buyer he had been preparing to grovel to all morning was actually Jude had finally sunk in.","\"Mr. Lawson! Jude! Wait, please!\" Sterling begged, his voice trembling as he stopped a few feet away, bowing so low his head nearly touched his knees. \"Trent Belmont is a powerful man, he pressured me to kick you out! I didn’t want to do it! Please, I have a mortgage, I have a family!\"","Jude slowly turned around.","\"You didn’t care about my rent when you fired me,\" Jude said. \"And you didn’t care about the truth when you let a spoiled heir humiliate me on this very floor. You are fired, Sterling.\"","\"Please, sir!\" Sterling sobbed, his knees buckling.","\"You have exactly ten minutes to clear out your desk before I have the security team throw you onto the street,\" Jude commanded. \"Get out of my sight.\"","Sterling let out a pathetic whimper. He looked around at the staff, hoping for someone to intervene, but they all immediately looked away.","Defeated, and realizing his career was destroyed, Sterling dragged himself toward the back offices.","Jude turned his attention to the rest of the staff.","He locked eyes with Maya, who was standing frozen near the receptionist’s desk. She looked terrified.","\"Maya, come here,\" Jude said.","Maya swallowed hard, taking a few hesitant steps forward. She was convinced she was about to be fired next.","\"M-Mr. Lawson... I... congratulations on your...\"","\"You were the only person in this building who treated me with an ounce of respect,\" Jude interrupted, his tone softening slightly. \"You covered my shifts when I was sick, and you actually bothered to learn my name.\"","Maya stared at him, bewildered. \"I just... it was the right thing to do.\"","\"And now it’s paying off,\" Jude smiled. \"Starting right now, you are the new General Manager of Zenith Motors. I’ll have Victoria draft a new contract doubling your previous salary. The floor is yours to run as you see fit.\"","Maya’s jaw hit the floor. The rest of the staff stared at her with burning envy.","\"Me?\" Maya gasped.","A general manager position at a high-end dealership came with a life-changing salary and massive commission overrides.","\"Jude... Mr. Lawson I don’t know what to say.\"","Before Maya could thank him again, Victoria stepped up next to Jude, covering her phone’s microphone with her hand.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" Victoria whispered. \"I just received a call from the front gate. The representatives from Belmont Enterprises have arrived for their scheduled real estate expansion meeting with the ’new owner’.\"","Jude’s smile widened into a grin.","He turned toward the doors just as a black sedan pulled up to the curb.","Arthur Belmont stepped out of the passenger side, adjusting his tie and looking incredibly serious.","A moment later, Trent Belmont stepped out of the driver’s side, looking exhausted but desperate to impress his father.","Neither of them had any idea that they were walking directly into the lion’s den...","\"Perfect timing,\" Jude murmured, turning to Maya. \"Clear the conference room. I have some guests.\""]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: The New Landlord","paragraphs":["Arthur Belmont stood on the pavement, staring up at the facade of Zenith Motors. He took a deep breath, smoothing down the lapels of his suit.","\"Listen to me very carefully, Trent,\" Arthur said. \"The Obsidian Conglomerate has ghosted my calls. Our company’s stock is already beginning to dip. Securing the real estate contracts for the Zenith expansion is our last lifeline. The man we are about to meet just dropped tens of millions of dollars to acquire this facility in a single morning. He is a shark. Do not speak unless spoken to. Do not make eye contact unless prompted. Do you understand me?\"","Trent swallowed hard. \"I understand, Dad. I won’t mess this up.\"","Arthur gave a nod, and the two of them walked through the sliding doors into the main showroom.","Before Arthur could approach the reception desk, Victoria stepped out from the main corridor.","\"Mr. Belmont?\" Victoria asked.","\"Yes, that’s me,\" Arthur replied, putting on his most charming smile. \"And this is my son, Trent. We are here for the real estate negotiation with the new owner.\"","Victoria offered a brief nod. \"I am Victoria, Senior Counsel. Please, follow me.\"","Arthur’s smile faltered slightly as he recognized the name. He leaned close to Trent as they followed her toward the staircase.","\"Vance & Sterling M&A. This billionaire retained one of the most ruthless corporate law firms in the state. We need to be flawless today.\"","Trent nodded, his anxiety spiking.","Victoria led them up the stairs and down a short hallway, stopping in front of the double doors of the executive suite. She pushed them open, gesturing for the two men to enter.","The boardroom was spectacular...","A long table stretched across the center of the room, flanked by plush leather chairs.","At the far end of the table, a high-backed CEO chair was turned around, facing the floor-to-ceiling window that overlooked the showroom below.","Arthur could only see the silhouette of the man sitting in the chair.","Arthur felt a bead of sweat roll down his spine. He stepped forward and offered a bow.","\"Good morning, sir,\" Arthur said. \"I am Arthur Belmont, CEO of Belmont Enterprises. This is my son, Trent. We are incredibly honored that you took the time to meet with us on your first day of ownership.\"","The chair slowly swiveled around.","Jude sat comfortably, one leg crossed over the other, holding a glass of sparkling water.","He looked at the two men, an amused smile playing on his lips.","\"Good morning, Arthur,\" Jude said, taking a slow sip of his water.","Trent stopped breathing.","His eyes bugged out of his head, his jaw dropping so fast it practically unhinged.","\"Jude?!\" Trent shrieked, losing whatever shred of composure he had left.","Arthur blinked, bewildered. He recognized the face immediately...","It was the struggling actor from the viral video they had mocked in the boardroom just an hour ago.","Trent’s fear instantly boiled over into outrage. He took two steps forward, pointing a finger at Jude. \"Are you out of your mind?! What the hell are you doing in the boss’s chair? Did you break in here to pull some kind of sick prank?\"","Jude just set his glass down on the table.","\"Get out of that seat right now!\" Trent yelled, his voice cracking. \"If the new owner walks in here and catches you pulling a stunt like this, he is going to have you thrown in a cell! Do you have any idea who you are dealing with?!\"","Arthur’s face darkened with fury. He assumed this was some sort of elaborate joke set up by the staff.","\"Listen to me, young man. I don’t know how you slipped past security, but this is a multi-million-dollar negotiation. Where is the real owner of this establishment?\"","Jude rested his elbows on the armrests, interlacing his fingers. \"You’re looking at him.\"","Trent burst into a hysterical laugh. His body actually shook with the force of it. It took him ten seconds to calm down.","\"Oh, man, you really had me for a second,\" Trent gasped, wiping a tear from his eye. \"You? The billionaire buyer? Yeah, right. You were literally washing tires yesterday. We all know you’re just some broke loser who got hired to do a viral marketing stunt for a suit company. You don’t have a dime to your name.\"","Jude just watched him laugh.","\"I don’t know what you’re trying to prove,\" Trent sneered, feeling a sudden surge of confidence. \"But the joke is over. Get out of the office before I call the cops myself.\"","Before Trent could reach for his phone, the doors of the boardroom swung open.","Victoria walked in, carrying a fresh pot of coffee and a stack of finalized legal documents.","She ignored the Belmonts, walking straight to the head of the table and pouring a cup of coffee for Jude.","\"The final transfer of the land deeds has cleared the state registry, Mr. Lawson,\" Victoria said, her tone laced with respect. \"You are officially the sole proprietor of this entire city block.\"","Arthur froze.","\"Wait,\" Arthur stammered, looking from Victoria to Jude. \"Ms. Vance... why are you playing along with this? This man is an actor. He’s a nobody.\"","Victoria paused, looking at Arthur as if he had just spoken a different language.","Her expression shifted into one of profound pity. \"Mr. Belmont, I am a Senior Partner at one of the most prestigious corporate law firms on the East Coast. I assure you, I do not ’play along’ with anyone. Mr. Lawson executed a hostile takeover of this facility at seven o’clock this morning using eight figures of liquid capital. He is the owner.\"","Trent’s legs gave out. He stumbled backward, his hip crashing into the edge of the table just to keep himself upright.","A moment later, Maya walked into the room, holding a tray with additional documents.","\"Excuse me, Mr. Lawson,\" Maya said, bowing her head slightly. \"I have the expansion blueprints you requested for the new lots.\"","\"Thank you, Maya,\" Jude said. \"Just leave them on the table.\"","Arthur’s mind scrambled to process the impossible reality playing out in front of him.","The lawyer confirmed it. The General Manager confirmed it.","The viral video was real. Jude really had dropped half a million dollars on clothes.","The billionaire VIP residing in the Obsidian Grand’s Presidential Suite was Jude.","Jude picked up his coffee cup, blowing the steam away. He looked into Trent’s eyes, his smile returning.","\"Now then,\" Jude said. \"I believe we have some real estate to discuss.\""]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: A $50 Million Great-Uncle","paragraphs":["\"Mr. Lawson,\" Arthur began, his voice stripped of its former arrogance. \"Please. I understand there has been a terrible misunderstanding between you and my son. But Belmont Enterprises has spent months surveying the expansion lots for Zenith Motors. We are prepared to offer highly favorable terms—\"","\"The expansion is cancelled,\" Jude interrupted, setting his coffee cup down.","Arthur’s breath hitched. \"Cancelled? Sir, please, if you just review the—\"","\"I have no intention of partnering with Belmont Enterprises,\" Jude said, his gaze shifting to Trent, who was staring at the floor. \"Your son made it abundantly clear that my presence was an eyesore. I wouldn’t want to tarnish your prestigious family image with my business. Victoria, have security escort them off my property.\"","\"Immediately,\" Victoria said, tapping an icon on her tablet.","Arthur tried to plead again, but the heavy boardroom doors swung open, and two burly security guards stepped inside.","Trent didn’t say a word. He looked thoroughly broken.","Without protesting, father and son were marched out of the executive suite, their future entirely destroyed.","Maya let out a long breath. She looked down at the real estate portfolios in her hands, then looked up at Jude, who was leaning back in the CEO chair.","\"Jude... Mr. Lawson...\" Maya started, her mind spinning with a thousand unanswered questions. \"I just... I don’t understand. What is going on? Are you secretly from a wealthy family? Were you hiding this from us the entire time you worked here?\"","Jude shook his head, offering a smile. \"I didn’t lie to anyone, Maya. I was exactly the broke, struggling guy you thought I was. You know I couldn’t even afford to buy lunch at the cafeteria most days.\"","\"Then how?\" Maya asked, her voice filled with disbelief. \"How did you buy a multi-million dollar dealership overnight?\"","Victoria, standing near the window, quietly adjusted her glasses.","She was equally intrigued. Her firm had executed the takeover, but the origin of Jude’s massive liquid capital was a complete mystery even to her...","Jude knew he couldn’t tell them the truth.","Explaining that a Universal Sign-In System had magically deposited tens of millions of dollars into his bank account simply by visiting a hotel and an alleyway would get him locked in a psychiatric ward.","He needed a believable cover story.","\"It’s a bizarre situation,\" Jude said. \"To put it simply, I was recently contacted by a great-uncle I never knew existed. He is an incredibly private, overseas investor. He caught wind of my financial struggles, tracked me down, and decided to give me a little starter capital to get me on my feet.\"","Maya’s eyes went wide. \"Starter capital?\"","\"He said it wasn’t much,\" Jude continued, waving his hand. \"He told me to spend it carefully. I checked the account balance he set up for me... he gave me fifty million dollars.\"","Maya felt dizzy. She had to grip the back of a chair to steady herself.","Fifty million dollars? As pocket change? Just to get on his feet?!","\"Good heavens,\" Maya breathed, her mind completely blown. \"How rich is your great-uncle?\"","\"Very,\" Jude replied smoothly. \"Though he values his privacy above all else.\"","\"What is his name, if you don’t mind me asking?\" Victoria chimed in.","Jude didn’t miss a beat. \"Elias Sterling. But he operates through shell corporations. You won’t find him on any Forbes list.\"","*Elias Sterling,* Victoria repeated internally, her eyes gleaming with sudden ambition.","It all made sense now...","Victoria had found it incredibly strange that a young, former retail worker possessed the ruthless business acumen to execute a hostile takeover so flawlessly.","Jude was clearly just a frontman, a proxy for this mysterious billionaire uncle, Elias Sterling!","Victoria’s heart raced.","If her firm could uncover the true identity of Elias Sterling and secure him as a direct client, it would be the biggest acquisition in the history of Vance & Sterling.","She needed to put her best investigators on this immediately.","Jude noticed Victoria’s calculating expression and smiled inwardly. The bait had been taken perfectly.","\"Victoria,\" Jude said. \"Could you give us the room for a moment? I need to speak with my new General Manager privately.\"","\"Of course, Mr. Lawson,\" Victoria said, giving a bow before exiting the boardroom.","The doors clicked shut, leaving Jude and Maya entirely alone in the executive suite.","Jude stood up from the leather chair and walked around the table.","Maya looked down at the floor, suddenly feeling incredibly small.","The reality of Jude’s new status was creating a terrifying gap between them.","\"Jude, I’m so sorry,\" Maya whispered. \"I’m sorry I couldn’t stop Sterling from firing you. I tried to argue with him in the back office, but he threatened to terminate me too.\"","Tears began to well in her eyes. The dealership had been a toxic place to work for years, and the constant fear of losing her livelihood had worn her down to the bone.","Jude stepped forward and placed his hands on her shoulders.","\"You have nothing to apologize for, Maya,\" Jude said. \"You were the only one who showed me kindness when I was at the absolute bottom. I know how much you sacrificed just to survive in this building.\"","Hearing the genuine warmth in his voice, Maya could no longer hold it back.","A quiet sob escaped her lips, and she leaned forward, resting her forehead against his chest.","Jude didn’t pull away. He wrapped his arms around her in a comforting embrace.","Maya cried silently against his suit, the years of accumulated anxiety, the fear of Sterling’s wrath, and the sheer relief of her sudden promotion all crashing down on her at once.","\"I was so scared,\" Maya whispered into his chest. \"I thought Sterling was going to ruin all of us.\"","\"Sterling is gone,\" Jude murmured, patting her back. \"And as long as I own this company, no one is ever going to bully you, or threaten your job, ever again. You are under my protection now.\"","Maya nodded against him. She felt an overwhelming sense of safety wrapped in his arms.","After a long moment, Maya pulled back, wiping her eyes and offering a watery smile. \"Thank you, Jude. I won’t let you down. I promise.\"","\"I know you won’t,\" Jude smiled, walking back toward the window overlooking the showroom.","He looked down at the floor. \"Now, tell me about the Belmonts. Why was Arthur sweating through his suit when I cancelled the expansion?\"","Maya composed herself, stepping up to the window beside him.","\"Belmont Enterprises is drowning in debt,\" Maya explained. \"They heavily over-leveraged their assets on residential projects that failed. Securing the commercial real estate contracts for our dealership’s statewide expansion was their only way to satisfy their creditors. Without our contracts, they will default on their loans.\"","Jude looked out at the city skyline, a dark gleam in his eyes.","Trent Belmont had humiliated him. Chloe had abandoned him and mocked his poverty.","They had both thought they were untouchable because of the Belmont fortune. But with a single signature, Jude had just severed their corporate lifeline..."]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: Signing in at the Slums","paragraphs":["The rest of the morning passed in a whirlwind of high-level transitions...","Jude spent an hour with Maya, outlining his vision for the dealership’s future.","Jude stepped out into the midday sun and slid into the backseat of his waiting Maybach.","\"Back to the Obsidian Grand, Mr. Lawson?\" the driver asked, glancing at Jude through the rearview mirror.","\"No,\" Jude replied, staring out the tinted window. \"Take me to the Southside. The Elm Street apartments.\"","The driver blinked, clearly caught off guard.","The Southside was a decaying, high-crime district, filled with crumbling infrastructure and cramped, low-income housing.","It was no place for a multi-million-dollar vehicle...","\"Sir? Are you certain?\" the driver asked hesitantly.","\"Just drive,\" Jude said.","Thirty minutes later, the luxury car rolled to a stop in front of a dilapidated, brick apartment complex.","The contrast was staggering. The Maybach looked like a spaceship that had landed in a junkyard.","Jude stepped out, ignoring the stares of the few locals lingering on the cracked sidewalk, and walked up the stairwell to the third floor.","He stopped in front of door 3B. Pinned to the cheap wood was a pink eviction notice.","Suddenly, a familiar chime echoed in his skull.","[Ding!]","[A new day has arrived. Would the host like to Sign-In?]","Jude smiled. The timing was perfect. He leaned against the peeling wallpaper of the hallway. \"Sign in.\"","[Sign-In Successful! Location: Southside Elm Apartments.]","[Location Evaluation: Very Low.]","[However, the Host has triggered a specialized real estate reward!]","[Reward: The deed to the Apex Commercial District (120 Acres).]","[The deed and transfer paperwork have been deposited into your System Inventory and registered with the city council.]","Jude froze.","The Apex Commercial District?","Even when he was scrubbing tires, Jude had heard about the Apex land.","It was a massive, undeveloped plot of prime real estate sitting right in the heart of the city’s financial sector.","It was considered the holy grail of urban development...","For years, massive conglomerates had tried to buy it, but it was permanently locked up in bureaucratic red tape and zoning disputes.","No one could buy it. It was completely untouchable.","And now, the system had just handed him the deed on a silver platter.","Before Jude could fully process the sheer magnitude of the reward, his phone vibrated in his pocket. It was Victoria.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" Victoria began. \"I am reviewing the expansion blueprints you left with me. If Zenith Motors is going to expand its footprint as aggressively as you want, we are going to need a massive plot of commercial land. Unfortunately, the Belmonts had the only viable lots.\"","\"Find another one,\" Jude said, stepping away from his apartment door.","\"It isn’t that simple, sir,\" Victoria sighed. \"The only other plot capable of housing a project of this scale is the Apex Commercial District. But it’s dead land. The city council has refused to sell it for over a decade. It’s notoriously impossible to acquire. I’ll have to start looking at suburban options outside the city limits.\"","Jude chuckled. \"Don’t bother looking outside the city, Victoria. We’ll use the Apex District.\"","There was a long silence on the other end of the line.","\"Sir?\" Victoria asked, her voice faltering. \"I just explained, the Apex land cannot be bought. The mayor himself couldn’t force that sale.\"","\"It doesn’t need to be bought,\" Jude said, pulling a folder out of his System Inventory that had materialized in his jacket pocket. \"I already hold the deed. I’ll have a courier send the paperwork to your office within the hour. Draft the construction permits.\"","Victoria literally dropped her pen.","\"You... you own the Apex District?\" Victoria stammered.","How was that even possible?","Getting that land required a level of political and financial influence that practically defied logic.","\"Take care of the permits, Victoria,\" Jude said, hanging up the phone.","Back in her office, Victoria stared at her phone screen, feeling lightheaded.","Shaking herself out of her stupor, she immediately dialed a highly encrypted number.","A gruff voice answered on the second ring. \"Victoria. Tell me you have an update.\"","\"I do, Richard,\" Victoria said, speaking to the senior managing partner of her law firm. \"I just finished the Zenith takeover. But there is something much bigger going on here.\"","\"Explain.\"","\"Jude Lawson is a proxy,\" Victoria said. \"He slipped up and gave me a name. Elias Sterling. An estranged, ultra-private billionaire relative. I believe Elias is the true mastermind behind this capital. Richard... he just informed me that he holds the deed to the Apex Commercial District.\"","Richard gasped audibly over the line. \"Apex? That’s impossible.\"","\"I thought so too,\" Victoria said. \"But he has it. Keep the investigation quiet, but we need to find Elias. If we can secure him as a direct client, our firm will be untouchable.\"","\"Brilliant work, Victoria,\" Richard praised. \"Keep Jude Lawson happy. Give him whatever he wants. We will find Elias.\"","Victoria hung up, feeling incredibly proud of her deduction.","At that exact moment, across town in the Belmont Enterprises headquarters...","Arthur Belmont was standing at the head of his boardroom, his face gray with exhaustion. Trent was sitting in the corner, holding his head in his hands.","\"Listen to me,\" Arthur said, slamming his palm against the table to command the attention of his executives. \"Yes, we lost the Zenith Motors expansion. But we are not dead yet.\"","The executives looked up, desperate for a shred of hope.","\"We still have our bid in for the Apex Commercial District,\" Arthur declared, his voice rising with confidence. \"I know it’s a long shot. I know the city council has been stonewalling it for years. But if we can grease the right palms and acquire even a fraction of that land, the creditors will back off. It is our final play.\"","A junior executive sitting near the door suddenly let out a strangled gasp, his face turning white as he stared at his laptop screen.","\"Sir...\" the executive whispered, his voice trembling so violently he could barely form the words.","\"What is it?\" Arthur snapped. \"Speak up!\"","The executive turned his laptop around. Displayed on the screen was a breaking news alert from the city’s real estate registry.","\"The Apex Commercial District...\" the executive swallowed hard. \"It... it was just sold, sir. The city council transferred the deed ten minutes ago to an anonymous private buyer. It’s gone.\"","\"WHAT?!\" Arthur roared, his voice cracking.","He lunged forward, grabbing the laptop. He stared at the screen, his eyes scanning the government transfer notice.","The land was gone... Their final safety net had vanished.","Arthur’s knees gave out. He collapsed into his chair, the laptop sliding out of his grip and crashing onto the floor.","Belmont Enterprises was finished."]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14: Opening Platinum Reward Box","paragraphs":["Arthur stared blankly at the ceiling of his boardroom.","\"Trace the filing,\" Arthur croaked.","He grabbed the edge of the table. \"Who filed the transfer deed with the city council? There has to be a public record of the legal firm representing the anonymous buyer!\"","The junior executive typed on a backup tablet.","A few seconds later, he swallowed hard. \"Sir... the legal firm listed on the city council’s ledger is Vance & Sterling Mergers and Acquisitions.\"","Arthur felt his heart stop.","Vance & Sterling.","There was only one client that firm was representing in real estate transactions this morning.","The billionaire VIP at the Obsidian Grand. The man who had just bought Zenith Motors. The man Trent had humiliated.","Jude Lawson.","Arthur lunged for the conference phone in the center of the table and punched in Victoria’s office line, praying it would forward to her mobile.","Back in the executive suite at Zenith Motors, Victoria was reviewing the dealership’s payroll when her phone vibrated on the desk.","She glanced at the caller ID and raised an eyebrow. \"Mr. Lawson. It’s Arthur Belmont. He’s calling my direct line.\"","Jude leaned back in his chair, swirling the sparkling water in his glass. \"Put him on speaker.\"","Victoria tapped the screen, and Arthur’s frantic breathing instantly echoed through the office.","\"Victoria! Please, tell me Mr. Lawson is with you!\" Arthur begged. He sounded like a man drowning. \"I know he bought the Apex Commercial District! I know he holds the deed!\"","\"I am here, Arthur,\" Jude said.","\"Mr. Lawson! Jude! Please!\" Arthur sobbed into the receiver. \"You have to listen to me! I will personally drag Trent to your office and make him scrub your floors if that’s what you want! Just lease us ten acres of the Apex District! Just a fraction of it! We will give you seventy percent of the developmental profits! If we don’t get that land, the bank is going to liquidate our family trust!\"","Jude took a sip of his water, letting the silence stretch for several seconds.","\"I bought the Apex District to build a private, high-speed test track for Zenith’s luxury hypercars,\" Jude said. \"I have no intention of leasing it to a failing residential firm. If you want a piece of that land, Arthur, you are welcome to buy it from me for triple the current market rate.\"","Arthur choked. Triple the market rate? It would cost hundreds of millions of dollars. He didn’t even have a fraction of that in liquid capital.","\"I... I can’t afford that,\" Arthur whispered. \"You’re killing my family, Jude.\"","\"Your family killed themselves,\" Jude corrected. \"Have a good afternoon, Arthur.\"","Victoria tapped the screen, cutting the line dead.","The dealership office was silent. Maya stared at Jude, her eyes wide.","Victoria couldn’t hide her admiration. Her eyes gleamed as she looked at her client.","[Ding!]","A chime echoed in Jude’s mind, cutting through his thoughts.","[Hidden Objective Completed: Corporate Retribution.]","[Reward: $100,000,000 USD.]","[Reward: Platinum System Reward Box x1.]","Jude’s phone buzzed in his pocket. He pulled it out and glanced at the push notification from Apex National Bank.","A hundred million dollars had just been seamlessly routed into his private accounts.","He had spent over half a million dollars on clothes and watches this morning.","He hadn’t even batted an eye at the cost, but now, seeing the system deposit one hundred million dollars into his account as a bonus reward, the spending felt entirely laughable...","He was earning money exponentially faster than he could ever hope to spend it.","\"Victoria, Maya,\" Jude said, standing up from his chair and buttoning his bespoke blazer. \"Cancel your afternoon appointments. I am taking my legal counsel and my new General Manager out for lunch.\"","Twenty minutes later, they were seated at a highly exclusive, Michelin-starred rooftop restaurant in the heart of the Zenith District.","Jude ordered the most expensive items on the menu without looking at the prices.","Plates of incredibly rare A5 Wagyu beef, butter-poached king crab, and truffles shaved over handmade pasta were presented to the table by a legion of bowing waiters.","Maya took a bite of the Wagyu. \"Oh my god... this is incredible. I’ve never tasted anything like this in my entire life.\"","Victoria nodded, delicately cutting a piece of crab. \"A phenomenal choice, Mr. Lawson. This establishment usually requires a six-month reservation. Having them clear the rooftop for us on twenty minutes’ notice is a testament to your influence.\"","Jude smiled, taking a sip of the vintage wine the sommelier had begged him to try.","The food was spectacular...","\"I’ll have my assistant set up a corporate account for you here, Maya,\" Jude said. \"If you’re going to be entertaining high-end clients for Zenith Motors, you should bring them here.\"","Maya’s face flushed with gratitude. \"Thank you, Jude. Truly. I will work incredibly hard for you. I won’t let this dealership fail.\"","\"I know you won’t,\" Jude said.","The lunch lasted for nearly two hours. Jude paid the bill without a second thought, leaving a tip that made the waiter literally burst into tears of joy.","After ensuring Maya and Victoria were safely escorted back to their respective offices by private drivers, Jude returned to the Obsidian Grand Hotel.","He walked into the living room of the Presidential Suite and sat down on the sofa.","It was finally time to see what the system had given him.","\"Open the Platinum Reward Box,\" Jude commanded.","[Opening Platinum System Reward Box...]","[Congratulations, Host! You have received 4 Rewards.]","[Acquired Skill Upgrade: Flawless Charisma (Passive).]","[Acquired Skill Upgrade: Absolute Appraisal (Passive).]","[Acquired Asset: 100% Controlling Stake in Apex Media Group.]","[Acquired Asset: $50,000,000 USD Offshore Investment Fund.]","Jude blinked.","*Absolute Appraisal: A passive ocular ability that allowed him to instantly determine the true market value, authenticity, and hidden flaws of any item or corporate asset he looked at.","*Flawless Charisma: An aura enhancement that commanded absolute respect, ensuring that any business negotiation or social interaction skewed heavily in his favor.","Jude could already feel the changes. His vision sharpened, colors becoming impossibly vivid, and a calm confidence settled deep into his bones.","But it was the third reward that made him raise an eyebrow.","Apex Media Group?","He pulled out his phone and quickly searched the name.","Apex Media Group was a multi-billion-dollar entertainment conglomerate.","They owned the largest television networks, movie studios, and talent agencies on the East Coast!"]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15: Late Night Planning","paragraphs":["Jude tapped his fingers against the armrest of the sofa, his mind working rapidly.","Owning a media conglomerate was a different beast than running a dealership, but the fifty million dollars sitting in an offshore investment fund was a much more immediate concern...","Capital that sat idle was capital wasted.","He picked up his phone and dialed Victoria’s number. She answered on the first ring.","\"Mr. Lawson. How can I assist you this evening?\"","\"I need your firm to leverage its network,\" Jude said. \"I have fifty million dollars in liquid offshore funds that I want to park in high-yield foreign trade projects. Reach out to the top-tier corporate families in your circle. Find out who needs massive capital injections, and set up the pitch meetings for tomorrow.\"","There was a sharp intake of breath on the other end of the line.","Fifty million in liquid cash was an astronomical sum to drop on a moment’s notice.","\"Furthermore,\" Jude added, \"I want a full dossier on the current executive board of Apex Media Group.\"","\"Apex Media?\" Victoria’s composure cracked slightly. \"Sir, they are the largest entertainment conglomerate in the region. Their valuation is staggering.\"","\"I know,\" Jude said. \"I just acquired a one hundred percent controlling stake. Find me those investment projects, Victoria. We have a busy day tomorrow.\"","He hung up the phone before she could even formulate a response.","Across the city, Victoria stared at her phone screen in disbelief.","Apex Media Group? Her mind raced.","The sheer scale of Jude’s acquisitions was terrifying...","She immediately began dialing the private numbers of the most elite corporate families in the state, informing them that a titan was looking to invest.","The response was instantaneous... everyone wanted a piece of Jude Lawson’s capital.","Back in the Presidential Suite, Jude opened his banking application.","He stared at the screen, watching the numbers reflect his total liquid assets.","Between the initial rewards and the bonus cash, his balance hovered over $150,000,000.","If he converted his assets and offshore accounts, his net worth was well into the billions...","He let out a low whistle, a genuine smile breaking across his face.","A soft knock at the suite’s double doors pulled him from his thoughts.","Jude stood up, straightening his loungewear, and pulled the doors open.","Victoria and Maya were standing in the hallway.","Both women had changed out of their strict business attire.","Victoria wore an elegant, form-fitting evening dress, and Maya was dressed in a stunning silk blouse and skirt that perfectly complemented her figure.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" Victoria smiled, stepping into the room. \"I brought the finalized deeds. And Maya insisted we bring something to celebrate.\"","\"I wanted to thank you properly,\" Maya said, her cheeks flushing slightly. \"Today changed my entire life. I thought we should toast to your empire.\"","Jude chuckled, stepping aside to let them in. \"I can’t say no to a celebration. Come in.\"","They moved into the living room of the suite. Jude popped the champagne, pouring three crystal flutes.","\"So,\" Maya said, a playful glint in her eye as she took a sip of champagne. \"Since we are off the clock, I propose a game.\"","\"A game?\" Jude asked, raising an eyebrow.","\"Corporate Truth or Dare,\" Victoria chimed in, leaning forward with a smile. \"We play a lot of it at the law firm. We draw cards. Whoever pulls the highest card gets to issue a command or ask a question. The catch is, you can’t refuse.\"","Jude smirked. \"Alright. Deal the cards.\"","Victoria pulled a sleek deck of playing cards from her designer purse... a staple for a lawyer who spent her life calculating odds.","She shuffled and dealt.","In the very first round, Maya pulled the King of Spades.","\"Ah,\" Maya smiled, her eyes darting between Victoria and Jude. \"I am the boss. Jude, since you own everything in the city... I dare you to maintain unbroken eye contact with Victoria for sixty seconds and tell her exactly what you look for in a partner.\"","Jude chuckled. It was a bold move...","He realized almost immediately that Maya and Victoria were subtly teaming up to test his composure.","He turned to Victoria, locking eyes with her.","The *Flawless Charisma* aura activated instantly.","Jude’s gaze was so intense, so magnetic, that Victoria actually felt her breath catch in her throat.","He calmly and smoothly described a partner who possessed absolute loyalty and ambition, never once breaking eye contact.","By the time the sixty seconds were up, Victoria’s face was flushed red, and she had to look away to compose herself.","\"Well played,\" Victoria muttered, fanning herself slightly.","The game continued. In the second round, Victoria pulled the Ace...","She immediately turned her sights on Jude. \"My turn. Mr. Lawson, I dare you to kiss Maya on the cheek. And Maya, you aren’t allowed to pull away.\"","Maya’s eyes went wide, her face turning a shade of crimson. \"Victoria!\"","\"Those are the rules,\" Victoria teased, leaning back into the sofa.","Jude shook his head.","He leaned forward, closing the distance between himself and Maya.","As he leaned in, Maya actually turned her head slightly, closing the gap faster than he anticipated.","His lips brushed against her cheek. When he pulled back, Maya looked flustered.","Victoria dealt the cards for the third round, her eyes locked onto Jude, eager to see how far they could push the billionaire.","Jude looked at his card, then tossed it onto the coffee table face down.","\"Alright, that’s enough,\" Jude said. He stood up, checking his platinum Audemars Piguet. \"It’s getting incredibly late, and we have a fifty-million-dollar investment marathon starting tomorrow morning. I need my General Counsel and my General Manager operating at absolute peak performance.\"","Victoria and Maya blinked.","\"Of course, Mr. Lawson,\" Victoria said, quickly recovering her composure. She stood up, smoothing her dress.","Maya nodded, though a clear flash of disappointment crossed her face. \"You’re right. Tomorrow is a big day.\"","Jude walked them to the double doors of the suite, offering them both a smile. \"Goodnight, ladies. Have your drivers text me when you get home safely.\"","The doors clicked shut behind them.","Out in the hallway of the Obsidian Grand, Victoria and Maya stood in silence for a long moment.","\"He didn’t even break a sweat,\" Maya whispered, bewildered. \"I thought we had him cornered.\""]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16: A Mission?","paragraphs":["The next morning...","Jude stretched, feeling incredibly rested, and picked up the tablet on his nightstand to order room service.","As the hotel staff wheeled the silver carts into his suite, a familiar chime echoed in his mind.","[Ding!]","[Due to the Host successfully completing a Hidden Objective yesterday, you have been awarded three Bonus Daily Sign-Ins!]","Jude grinned. The system just kept giving. \"Sign in.\"","[Bonus Sign-In 1 Successful! Reward: $30,000,000 USD.]","[Bonus Sign-In 2 Successful! Reward: $40,000,000 USD.]","[Bonus Sign-In 3 Successful! Reward: $25,000,000 USD.]","His phone on the coffee table vibrated three times in rapid succession. Jude picked it up and opened his Apex National Bank app.","*Total Deposits Received: $95,000,000.00.*","Jude let out a laugh as he bit into his truffle omelet.","The breakfast he was eating cost nearly three thousand dollars... a sum that would have taken him a year to save just a few days ago.","Now? It was a microscopic fraction of a penny compared to the ninety-five million dollars that had just materialized in his account over a cup of coffee.","Just as he finished eating, Victoria called.","\"Good morning, Mr. Lawson,\" Victoria said.\"The Obsidian Grand’s private conference atrium is packed. I spent the entire night calling in favors. We have CEOs from top-tier foreign trade logistics, offshore tech startups, and international supply chains. They are all incredibly eager to pitch for your fifty-million-dollar fund.\"","\"Understood,\" Jude said casually, pouring himself a second cup of coffee. \"I’ll be down shortly.\"","\"Sir, they are getting a bit restless...\"","\"Let them wait, Victoria,\" Jude said smoothly. \"I hold the capital. They aren’t going anywhere.\"","He took his time, showering, dressing in a bespoke midnight-blue suit, and snapping his Audemars Piguet onto his wrist.","When Jude finally stepped out of the private elevator and approached the Grand Atrium, the noise was deafening.","Dozens of elite executives were pacing the room, adjusting their ties and rehearsing their pitches.","But the moment Jude walked through the double doors, flanked by Victoria, the room fell dead silent.","The silence only lasted for a second before the crowd swarmed him.","\"Mr. Lawson! It is a profound honor. My shipping conglomerate desperately needs liquid capital to open new ports in Europe!\"","\"Mr. Lawson! I represent an offshore tech manufacturing firm. If you invest your fifty million with us, we can guarantee a twenty percent return on investment by Q3!\"","\"Please, sir, our international supply chain is heavily discounted right now! We are the perfect asset!\"","Jude stood in the center of the chaos.","The desperation in the room was palpable...","They were practically begging him to take their equity.","Before Jude could even respond to the first pitch, the doors of the atrium were shoved open.","\"That’s enough!\" a harsh voice echoed across the room.","The crowd parted as a tal man in his late twenties stormed into the room, followed by a small army of private security and financial analysts.","Victoria leaned close to Jude. \"That is Damian Cross. He’s the heir to Cross Capital, a hundred-billion-dollar venture capital empire. They have a monopoly on foreign trade investments in this city.\"","Damian glared at the executives in the room, his face twisted in disgust. \"What is wrong with you people? You’re on your knees for a guy nobody had even heard of two days ago!\"","Damian then turned his glare onto Jude.","\"I don’t know who you are, Lawson, or where you got a fifty-million-dollar offshore fund,\" Damian sneered. \"But you do not waltz into my city and poach my clients. Cross Capital controls the foreign trade sector. If you think you can disrupt my family’s market share, I will ensure your fund is bled dry by the end of the month.\"","Jude looked at Damian.","Suddenly, a system notification flashed in Jude’s mind.","[Mission Triggered: Establish Absolute Financial Dominance.]","[Objective: The Host has been challenged by a rival financial entity. Assert dominance by investing over $200,000,000 USD in foreign projects today.]","[Reward: +1 Money Sign-In, +1 Platinum System Reward Box.]","Jude’s smile slowly crept onto his face.","A mission?","He had just been handed ninety-five million dollars this morning.","He had the fifty million offshore fund. And he had tens of millions sitting in his main checking account.","Spending two hundred million was going to be incredibly entertaining...","\"I don’t have a market share to protect, Damian,\" Jude said. \"I just woke up this morning feeling a bit bored, and decided I wanted to drop a few hundred million dollars to pass the time.\"","The entire room gasped.","Did he just say a *few hundred million*? To pass the time?!","The executives looked at Jude with wide eyes.","They thought he was only here to invest a fifty-million-dollar fund. If he had hundreds of millions to throw around casually, his true net worth had to be utterly astronomical.","Damian’s face flushed a deep red. He refused to be intimidated.","\"You have a big mouth,\" Damian laughed, a mocking sound. \"A few hundred million? Please. Cross Capital has already injected five hundred million dollars into the foreign market this year alone! Do you hear me? Five hundred million! You are nothing compared to a hundred-billion-dollar empire!\"","\"He’s right,\" one CEO whispered to another. \"Cross Capital just dropped four billion RMB on overseas infrastructure. They are untouchable.\"","\"If we side with this Lawson guy and he loses, Cross Capital will blacklist us forever,\" another executive muttered nervously.","Jude didn’t flinch at the staggering number. In fact, he looked disappointed.","\"Five hundred million dollars?\" Jude echoed, tilting his head slightly as he looked at the heir. \"Over the course of an entire year?\"","Damian’s sneer faltered slightly. \"Yes! More capital than you will ever see in your lifetime!\"","\"Damian, you might want to hire better accountants,\" Jude said, a smile touching his lips. \"Five hundred million spread across three hundred and sixty-five days is barely forty million a month. When you spread that across dozens of international subsidiaries, it’s basically pennies.\"","Damian’s face darkened.","\"You dare look down on Cross Capital?\" Damian hissed through gritted teeth. \"I’d love to see how much actual cash a nobody like you can produce without financing!\"","\"I’m glad you asked,\" Jude replied. He turned his attention to the crowd of executives. \"As of right now, I am officially raising my initial investment capital. I will be investing two hundred million dollars into your foreign trade assets before lunch.\"","The Grand Atrium went silent for a fraction of a second before erupting.","Two hundred million dollars? In a single morning?!"]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17: A Fake Banking App","paragraphs":["The executives abandoned their fear of Cross Capital, surging toward Jude and Victoria.","In the cutthroat world of foreign trade, immediate liquid capital was king...","A firm that could drop two hundred million dollars in cash on a Tuesday morning was a financial deity.","\"Mr. Lawson! Please, review my prospectus!\"","\"Sir, my logistics firm can absorb fifty million right now!\"","\"Mr. Lawson, over here!\"","Damian was shoved aside by a desperate tech CEO. He stumbled back, panic washing over him.","If this mysterious billionaire actually injected two hundred million dollars into the market today, Cross Capital’s influence over these companies would evaporate overnight.","\"You think you can outspend my family?\" Damian snarled, pulling his phone from his suit.","He marched to the corner of the atrium, furiously dialing his father, the CEO of Cross Capital. He needed the board to authorize an emergency war chest, right this second.","While Damian was panicking, Jude activated his newly acquired *Absolute Appraisal* skill.","Instantly, the world around him shifted. As he looked at the desperate executives shoving their portfolios into his hands, glowing lines of text hovered over their heads.","He looked at a man pitching a massive overseas real estate venture.","[Projected 5-Year ROI: -22%. Hidden Flaw: Severe structural debt.]","Jude passed him over without a second glance.","He scanned the crowd, his eyes darting from person to person until he spotted a nervous woman clutching a tablet.","[Overseas Microchip Logistics. Projected 5-Year ROI: +135%. Highly lucrative.]","\"You,\" Jude pointed to her. \"I’ll take forty percent of your equity for seventy million.\"","The woman burst into tears of joy.","Using his *Absolute Appraisal*, Jude selected two more companies with guaranteed returns over the next five years.","He didn’t care that he was dipping into his own personal cash reserves to supplement the fifty-million-dollar offshore fund. He knew the returns would be astronomical.","Victoria’s fingers flew across her laptop keyboard, drafting the rapid-fire investment contracts and executing the wire transfers directly from Jude’s accounts.","In less than twenty minutes, Jude had successfully deployed exactly two hundred million dollars!","[Ding!]","The chime rang out clearly in Jude’s mind.","[Mission Completed: Establish Absolute Financial Dominance.]","[Reward: +1 Money Sign-In, +1 Platinum System Reward Box.]","[Escalation Mission Triggered: Crush the Opposition.]","[Objective: The rival entity is currently mobilizing capital to counter the Host. Outspend and utterly humiliate the opposing firm.]","[Reward: +2 Money Sign-Ins, +1 Diamond System Reward Box!]","Jude’s eyes lit up. A Diamond Box?","\"Sign in,\" Jude thought.","[Money Sign-In Successful! Reward: $30,000,000 USD.]","The cash instantly hit his account, but Jude wasn’t focused on that. He immediately directed his attention to the Platinum Box he had just earned.","\"Open the Platinum Reward Box.\"","[Opening Platinum System Reward Box...]","[Calculating RNG...]","[CRITICAL SYSTEM EVENT! The Host has triggered a 3x Multiplier Explosion!]","[Acquired Asset: $150,000,000 USD Offshore Investment Fund.]","[Acquired Asset: $150,000,000 USD Offshore Investment Fund.]","[Acquired Asset: $150,000,000 USD Offshore Investment Fund.]","Jude’s breath hitched in his throat.","His phone vibrated in his pocket. He pulled it out, staring at the push notifications from his banking app.","Three separate, encrypted offshore wire transfers had just cleared into his portfolio.","Four hundred and fifty million dollars...","A total of four hundred and fifty million dollars had just been seamlessly deposited into his hands.","Jude stared at the series of zeros on his screen, blinded by the sheer scale of the wealth.","It was terrifying. He had spent two hundred million just minutes ago, and the system had instantly refunded him more than double.","Before Jude could even put his phone away, a loud laugh echoed across the atrium.","\"Alright! Everyone listen up!\"","Damian Cross marched back into the center of the room, looking incredibly smug.","\"The Cross Capital board of directors just held an emergency vote,\" Damian announced, making sure his voice carried over the murmurs of the crowd. \"And we have officially authorized an immediate liquidity injection of two hundred and fifty million dollars!\"","Several executives gasped.","To raise two hundred and fifty million dollars in liquid cash in under twenty minutes was a staggering display of corporate power..","Damian turned to Jude. \"Did you hear that, Lawson? Two hundred and fifty million. I told you that you couldn’t compete with a real legacy firm. You blew your two hundred million, and now Cross Capital is going to buy out the rest of the room. \"","Jude looked at Damian’s triumphant face, then let out a chuckle.","He slowly began to clap his hands.","\"I have to admit, Damian, that is a very impressive turnaround time for a dinosaur firm,\" Jude smiled, slipping one hand into his pocket. \"Two hundred and fifty million is a solid effort.\"","Damian frowned, sensing the lack of fear in Jude’s voice. \"It’s more than you have left.\"","\"Is it?\" Jude asked, pulling his phone back out and tapping the screen. \"Because my offshore accounts just cleared another automatic transfer.\"","Jude held the phone up, showing the banking screen to Damian and the executives standing nearby.","\"It’s not much,\" Jude sighed. \"Just another four hundred and fifty million dollars in liquid cash. Now... who else needs funding?\"","Dozens of the most powerful executives in the city stood frozen, their eyes locked on the screen of Jude’s phone.","Damian Cross stared at the screen. He blinked, rubbing his eyes as if the numbers were some kind of stress-induced hallucination.","\"That’s... that’s a mockup,\" Damian stammered. \"It’s a fake banking app! You expect me to believe a guy who came out of nowhere has half a billion in unfinanced cash just sitting on his phone? It’s a bluff!\"","Damian looked around the room, trying to rally the executives. \"Don’t fall for this, people! He’s a con artist! Cross Capital has real money! We have two hundred and fifty million ready to deploy right now!\"","A few of the executives shifted nervously, looking between Damian and Jude.","The Cross family legacy was a known, terrifying entity.","Jude let out a disappointed sigh. He slipped his phone back into the inner pocket of his suit."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18: Diamond Box","paragraphs":["\"You really don’t know when to fold, Damian,\" Jude said.","He turned his attention away from the heir and addressed the crowd of executives. \"Cross Capital just offered you a collective two hundred and fifty million dollars. Between that and their previous yearly investments, their total market influence hovers around seven hundred and fifty million.\"","\"I find this back-and-forth incredibly tedious,\" Jude announced. \"So, let’s end the game. I am currently holding two hundred million in finalized contracts. I am now opening a secondary capital pool. I will be investing an additional six hundred million dollars into your foreign trade assets before I leave this room.\"","The executives felt the air leave their lungs.","Six hundred million? On top of the two hundred million he had already spent?","That was an eight-hundred-million-dollar morning...","\"Victoria,\" Jude said, not breaking eye contact with the crowd. \"Prepare the wire transfers.\"","\"Yes, Mr. Lawson,\" Victoria replied, her fingers flying across her laptop keyboard.","Even as a senior partner who handled massive mergers, her heart was hammering against her ribs.","The brief hesitation the executives felt vanished in an instant. The atrium erupted into chaos.","\"Mr. Lawson! Please! Look at our European supply chain!\"","\"Sir, my biotech firm needs a hundred million! We can guarantee a fifty percent return!\"","\"Take my equity! Take sixty percent, I don’t care, just fund the offshore rigs!\"","The crowd of CEOs and presidents surged forward, abandoning all professional decorum.","Damian Cross was caught in the stampede.","A logistics magnate practically shoulder-checked him out of the way to get closer to Jude’s table.","Damian stumbled backward, his designer shoes skidding on the floor, and crashed hard into a decorative tree.","He scrambled to his feet. \"Wait! Cross Capital will blacklist you! We’ll freeze your domestic assets!\"","\"Shut up, Damian!\" an older CEO snapped, not even looking back at him. \"Mr. Lawson is speaking!\"","Damian’s jaw dropped. He had just been told to shut up by a man who had spent the last five years begging his father for funding. It was over... The Cross family monopoly was broken.","Jude ignored the scrambling and activated his *Absolute Appraisal*.","[European Automotive Export. Projected ROI: -12%. Hidden Flaw: Imminent labor strike.]","He ignored the man screaming for fifty million.","[Deep-Sea Telecom Cable Expansion. Projected ROI: +180%. Highly lucrative.]","\"You,\" Jude pointed to a tall woman in a grey suit. \"I’m taking a fifty-one percent controlling stake in your telecom expansion for two hundred million.\"","The woman gasped, tears literally springing to her eyes. \"Yes! Yes, absolutely, sir!\"","[South American Rare Earth Mining. Projected ROI: +210%. Generational Wealth Asset.]","\"The mining operation,\" Jude pointed to an older gentleman near the back. \"Three hundred million for a forty percent share.\"","The man nearly collapsed from relief, furiously nodding his head.","Jude quickly identified a third company and dropped the remaining one hundred million on them.","\"That’s six hundred million,\" Jude said smoothly. \"Victoria, execute the contracts.\"","\"Drafting the equity transfers now, sir,\" Victoria said, her voice shaking slightly. She hit the final keystroke. \"The funds are clearing the international registry. It is done.\"","Jude had successfully spent eight hundred million dollars in cash.","And thanks to his appraisal skill, the returns over the next few years were going to yield him billions.","He turned his gaze back to Damian Cross, who was still standing near the plant.","\"I believe we are finished here, Damian,\" Jude said. \"You can take your two hundred and fifty million back to your father. Tell him the foreign trade sector is under new management.\"","Damian opened his mouth to speak, to threaten, to salvage some shred of his dignity, but no words came out.","He turned on his heel and sprinted out of the atrium, followed closely by his bewildered security team.","The moment the doors swung shut behind Damian, a chime rang out clearly in Jude’s mind.","[Escalation Mission Completed: Crush the Opposition!]","[Cross Capital’s market dominance has been successfully usurped.]","[Reward: +2 Money Sign-Ins, +1 Diamond System Reward Box!]","Jude’s smile widened into a grin.","\"Sign in,\" Jude commanded.","[Bonus Sign-In 1 Successful! Reward: $40,000,000 USD.]","[Bonus Sign-In 2 Successful! Reward: $60,000,000 USD.]","With the capital officially distributed, the executives who hadn’t received funding realized that the window had closed.","But instead of leaving, they became even more desperate to secure Jude’s favor for the future.","\"Mr. Lawson!\" a shipping CEO pleaded, shoving a gold-embossed business card across the table. \"Please, allow me to host you on my yacht in Monaco next month! All expenses paid!\"","\"Jude, my private golf club in the Hamptons is entirely at your disposal!\" another executive shouted. \"I’ll waive the million-dollar entry fee today!\"","\"Mr. Lawson, my daughter is a runway model in Milan! You simply must let me introduce you two over dinner!\"","Now, with his *Flawless Charisma* grounding him, he found the display pathetic.","They were just chasing the money... They didn’t care about him.","Jude stood up, buttoning his jacket. \"Victoria, collect their contact information. If I require their services in the future, my office will reach out.\"","\"Of course, Mr. Lawson,\" Victoria said, stepping between Jude and the crowd. \"Gentlemen, please form a line. Mr. Lawson’s schedule is incredibly restricted.\"","Jude walked straight through the parting crowd, the executives bowing their heads as he passed, and exited the Grand Atrium.","He took the private elevator down to the underground VIP garage, where his driver was already waiting beside the black Maybach.","The driver opened the rear door. \"Where to, Mr. Lawson? Back to Zenith Motors?\"","\"No,\" Jude said, sliding into the cabin. \"Just drive. Take the scenic route out toward the coastline. I need some quiet.\"","\"Right away, sir.\"","The Maybach rolled out of the garage, blending into the mid-morning city traffic.","The tinted windows insulated Jude from the outside world.","Jude leaned back against the plush headrest and let out a long breath.","He had just humiliated a legacy billionaire, spent eight hundred million dollars, and secured a stranglehold on the city’s foreign trade sector, all before lunch.","But as exhilarating as the corporate warfare had been, Jude was far more interested in the notification glowing in the corner of his vision.","The Platinum Box had given him four hundred and fifty million dollars in a massive multiplier explosion, along with an entire media conglomerate.","He now possessed a Diamond Box.","\"System,\" Jude thought. \"Open the Diamond System Reward Box.\""]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19: A Private Island","paragraphs":["[Consuming Diamond System Reward Box...]","[Congratulations, Host! You have received three high-tier rewards!]","[Acquired Skill: Absolute Probability (Active).]","[Acquired Asset: Sapphire Cove Private Island.]","[Acquired Asset: Sovereign Maritime Rights (10 Square Nautical Miles).]","Jude blinked.","He focused on the skill first.","*Absolute Probability: An active ability that allows the Host to predict the outcome of any game of chance, lottery, or market fluctuation for exactly sixty seconds. This skill has a cooldown of twenty-four hours.","Jude couldn’t help but chuckle. It was an incredibly powerful ability... essentially turning him into an invincible gambler for one minute a day.","But with hundreds of millions of dollars sitting in his bank accounts and multiple thriving corporations under his control, stepping into a casino felt entirely redundant.","He didn’t need to gamble to make money anymore. Still, as a trump card for high-stakes negotiations, it was a safety net.","But it was the next two rewards that truly made his breath catch in his throat.","A private island?","Jude tapped the glowing folder icon in his system inventory, pulling up the digital deed.","Sapphire Cove was a legendary island located in the crystal-clear waters of the Caribbean.","But the system hadn’t just given him the land; it had secured a ten-square-nautical-mile maritime exclusion zone around the island.","He didn’t just own a piece of real estate... He owned a small sovereign nation!","\"Unbelievable,\" Jude muttered, shaking his head in awe.","Purchasing an island of that caliber, complete with private maritime rights, was something even the most entrenched billionaires couldn’t achieve with raw cash alone...","It required decades of maneuvering.","Before Jude could fully process the magnitude of his new tropical empire, his phone vibrated in his pocket.","It was a text from Victoria.","*Mr. Lawson. Seraphina Frost, the acting CEO of Apex Media Group, just contacted my office. She is requesting your immediate presence at Apex Tower. A rival studio head has infiltrated the executive boardroom and is attempting a hostile talent poach ahead of the annual summer gala.*","Jude raised an eyebrow. A hostile talent poach on his first day of ownership?","He tapped the partition dividing the Maybach’s cabin. \"Change of plans. Take me to Apex Tower in the media district.\"","\"Right away, Mr. Lawson,\" the driver replied, navigating the luxury car through the downtown traffic.","Twenty minutes later, Jude stepped out of the Maybach and walked into the lobby of Apex Media Group...","It was the epicenter of the city’s entertainment industry.","Digital billboards displayed the faces of A-list actors, chart-topping musicians, and blockbuster movie posters... all of which Jude now completely owned.","Jude bypassed the security desks and took the executive elevator directly to the top floor.","He approached the doors of the executive boardroom and pushed them open.","Sitting along the table were half a dozen of the country’s most famous, highly paid actresses and top-tier influencers.","At the head of the table stood Seraphina Frost, a brilliant woman in her late thirties who looked like she was currently fighting off a migraine.","And standing casually near the floor-to-ceiling windows, holding a glass of sparkling water and flashing a million-dollar smile, was a man Jude didn’t recognize.","\"Seraphina, you have to be realistic,\" the man was saying. \"Apex Media was just bought out by a complete unknown. Some phantom investor who probably wants to gut the studio for parts. Why on earth would you ladies tie your careers to a sinking ship?\"","Seraphina gritted her teeth. \"Donovan, you are trespassing in a private corporate meeting. I will call security.\"","\"Call them,\" Donovan Pierce laughed, unbothered.","He turned his attention to the A-list actresses. \"Pierce Studios is hosting our annual summer retreat next week. We aren’t doing some boring hotel gala in the city. My father pulled massive geopolitical strings, and we secured a fifty-person VIP invitation to Sapphire Cove.\"","The boardroom erupted in shocked gasps.","Even Seraphina’s eyes widened in disbelief.","\"Sapphire Cove?\" one of the lead actresses, a stunning woman named Chloe, asked breathlessly. \"I thought that island was locked down. Billionaires can’t even get clearance to sail past it!\"","\"Exactly,\" Donovan smirked, taking a slow sip of his water. \"It is the most exclusive piece of land on the planet. And Pierce Studios has exclusive access for the weekend. We are chartering a private mega-yacht to take our top talent. If you sign with my studio today, your name goes on that boarding pass. Crystal blue water, privacy, and the kind of prestige money can’t buy.\"","The actresses began whispering among themselves.","The allure of the island was intoxicating...","In the entertainment industry, prestige and exclusivity were the ultimate currencies.","Being seen at Sapphire Cove would elevate their careers to untouchable heights.","Seraphina looked defeated. She had been planning to host the Apex gala at a five-star hotel downtown.","It was a luxurious plan, but compared to a private island in the Caribbean, it was a joke. She was going to lose her top talent.","\"Excuse me,\" Jude said, stepping fully into the boardroom.","Every head in the room snapped toward the door.","Donovan Pierce looked Jude up and down, his smile faltering slightly at the presence Jude projected. \"Who are you? The new security guard?\"","Seraphina, however, recognized him instantly from the legal dossiers.","She stood up immediately, her posture rigid with respect. \"Mr. Lawson. I... I apologize for this intrusion. We are currently experiencing a disruption.\"","The actresses gasped again, their eyes locking onto Jude.","This was the mysterious billionaire who had acquired the entire conglomerate overnight?","\"Lawson?\" Donovan scoffed. \"Ah, the new money. Well, Mr. Lawson, you bought a sinking ship. Your top stars are leaving with me.\"","\"Is that so?\" Jude asked, walking toward the table.","\"You can’t compete,\" Donovan laughed, gesturing broadly to the room. \"What is Apex going to offer them for the summer gala? A ballroom at the Obsidian Grand? A nice dinner downtown? I’m offering them Sapphire Cove. You can have all the cash in the world, Lawson, but you don’t have the social capital to get past the maritime security of an island like that.\"","The actresses looked at Jude, their expressions a mix of pity and lingering desire for the island trip.","They wanted to stay with Apex, but Donovan’s offer was simply too legendary to pass up...","Seraphina closed her eyes, preparing for the inevitable wave of contract resignations.","Jude stood at the head of the table, looking at Donovan’s incredibly smug face.","He thought about the digital deed sitting quietly in his system inventory, complete with the ten-square-nautical-mile sovereign exclusion zone.","Donovan was bragging about begging his father for a temporary visitor’s pass to a piece of land that Jude literally owned.","A slow smile spread across Jude’s face.","\"A ballroom?\" Jude echoed, shaking his head. \"Seraphina, cancel the hotel reservations for the summer gala.\"","Seraphina blinked, confused. \"Cancel them, sir?\"","\"Yes,\" Jude said, his gaze locking onto Donovan’s suddenly nervous eyes. \"Apex Media won’t be renting a hotel. We’re taking the company jets to my private island.\""]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20: The Client","paragraphs":["Inside the Department of City Planning...","Commissioner Hayes slammed both of his hands onto his desk. He stared at his deputy commissioner as if the man had just grown a second head.","\"What did you just say?\" Hayes demanded. \"The Apex Commercial District was transferred? To a private buyer?!\"","The deputy flinched, taking a step back toward the door.","\"Commissioner, please,\" the deputy stammered. \"It was processed through the state registry this morning. The deed is gone.\"","\"That is impossible!\" Hayes roared, marching around the desk. \"That land has been locked in zoning disputes for a decade! The city council explicitly barred any sale of the Apex District without a unanimous vote! I never authorized this! Who forged the clearance?\"","The deputy wiped a bead of cold sweat from his forehead and opened the binder, flipping to the final page. \"Sir... nobody forged it. Without your permission, the registry software wouldn’t even accept the file. Look.\"","Hayes snatched the binder.","Right there, at the bottom of the irrevocable transfer deed, was his own signature.","The pressure of the pen, the slight slant of the letters... it was undeniably his handwriting.","Furthermore, his personal biometric seal was stamped right next to it!","Hayes stared at the paper, his mind blanking. \"When... when did I sign this?\"","\"I don’t know, sir,\" the deputy whispered nervously. \"A courier dropped the finalized paperwork off this morning. I assumed you pushed it through late last night during the council dinner.\"","Hayes felt a cold chill run down his spine. Had he drank too much at the dinner?","Had some smooth-talking lobbyist cornered him and slipped the paperwork onto his table?","He couldn’t remember a single detail... It was as if a blind spot had been inserted into his memory.","\"Who is the buyer?\" Hayes asked, his trembling. \"If the press finds out we sold the Apex District in the middle of the night, there will be a federal investigation!\"","Before the deputy could answer, the secure red telephone on Hayes’ desk began to ring.","Hayes stared at it in horror. It was the direct line to the Mayor’s office.","*I’m finished,* Hayes thought, his stomach dropping into his shoes. *The Mayor knows. I’m going to federal prison.*","With shaking hands, Hayes picked up the receiver. \"Mr. Mayor... I can explain the Apex transfer—\"","\"Hayes, you brilliant son of a gun!\" the Mayor’s booming, jovial voice interrupted. \"I was just about to call a council meeting to suggest we find a loophole for the Apex land, but you beat me to the punch! Great minds really do think alike!\"","Hayes froze, entirely stupified.","\"Sir?\" Hayes squeaked. \"You... you aren’t calling for my resignation?\"","\"Resignation? I’m putting you up for a commendation!\" the Mayor laughed heartily. \"Transferring that dead land to Jude Lawson was the smartest thing this city has done in twenty years! The man is a financial godsend!\"","Hayes blinked, lost. \"Jude Lawson?\"","\"You didn’t see the morning reports?\" the Mayor asked, his tone filled with awe. \"Lawson just executed a hostile takeover of Apex Media Group, and then dumped eight hundred million dollars in pure cash into our foreign trade sector. He is single-handedly propping up the city’s GDP! Keeping a titan like him happy is our top priority. Excellent work, Hayes!\"","The line clicked dead.","Hayes slowly lowered the phone, letting out a sigh of relief.","He looked up at his deputy, who was staring at him in equal disbelief.","\"This Jude Lawson...\" Hayes muttered, wiping the sweat from his brow. \"He drops eight hundred million in a single morning? The man must have limitless resources. Listen to me very carefully. Whatever Mr. Lawson wants to build on that land, you fast-track the permits. Do not put a single piece of red tape in his way. This man’s future is beyond anything we can calculate.\"","\"Yes, Commissioner!\" the deputy nodded fiercely.","***","Maxwell Cross, the billionaire CEO of the venture capital empire, hurled a whiskey tumbler against the wall of his office. It shattered into a thousand pieces.","Damian stood in the center of the room, looking down at his shoes, terrified of his father’s wrath.","\"Eight hundred million dollars!\" Maxwell roared, his face purple with rage. \"You let an absolute nobody walk into a room and publicly humiliate you! We lost our entire foreign trade monopoly in thirty minutes!\"","\"Dad, I didn’t know!\" Damian pleaded. \"He had limitless liquidity! And... and an insider at the planning bureau just texted me. Lawson acquired the Apex Commercial District this morning. He owns everything!\"","Maxwell gripped the edges of his desk, his knuckles turning white.","\"Lawson is a nobody,\" Maxwell hissed. \"A twenty-something kid does not orchestrate a billion-dollar financial coup overnight. He is a puppet on a string.\"","Damian looked up, confused. \"A puppet?\"","\"I have ears inside Vance & Sterling,\" Maxwell sneered, a cruel smile touching his lips. \"The lawyers are whispering. The real money backing Lawson belongs to an ultra-private, hidden billionaire named Elias Sterling. Lawson is just the public face.\"","Maxwell turned toward the floor-to-ceiling window, looking out over the city.","\"Elias Sterling,\" Maxwell muttered to himself. \"No matter how much money you have, or how well you hide in the shadows, you cannot usurp Cross Capital. I will find you, Elias. And I will destroy you.\"","Jude, of course, was unaware that the CEO of a hundred-billion-dollar empire had just declared a blood feud against a fake uncle he had made up on the spot yesterday afternoon...","And even if he had known, he wouldn’t have cared.","The system handled the impossible logistics, wiping memories and forging unassailable paper trails to ensure his rewards were completely bulletproof.","Right now, Jude was focused on his upcoming island getaway.","Sitting in the back of the Maybach, Jude reviewed a tablet Victoria had handed him.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" Victoria said from the seat opposite him. \"If we are genuinely relocating the Apex Media summer gala to Sapphire Cove, the logistical requirements are going to be monumental. We need to hire a mainland event-planning firm immediately to handle the VIP boarding, press management, and red-carpet transport before they get on your jets.\"","Jude swiped through the tablet. \"Who did you have in mind?\"","\"I strongly suggest the Vanguard Group,\" Victoria replied without hesitation. \"They are the premier event logistics firm in the state. They have guaranteed flawless execution.\"","\"No,\" Jude said smoothly, handing the tablet back. \"I don’t want Vanguard.\"","Victoria blinked in surprise. \"May I ask why? Who would you prefer?\"","\"Carmichael Events,\" Jude said, a smile playing on his lips.","Victoria frowned, quickly pulling up the registry on her laptop.","When she saw the financial profile of Carmichael Events, she looked at Jude as if he were insane.","\"Mr. Lawson... Carmichael Events is a tiny, boutique PR firm on the verge of bankruptcy,\" Victoria cautioned. \"They handle local weddings and minor corporate retreats. Giving them a multi-million-dollar entertainment gala is incredibly risky.\"","Jude just smiled.","He didn’t care about their logistics... He cared about the fact that the firm was owned and operated by Chloe’s mother, Evelyn Carmichael.","Evelyn was the woman who had endlessly berated Jude for his poverty.","She was the one who had convinced Chloe to break their engagement and chase after the wealthy Trent Belmont, calling Jude a \"worthless anchor\" who would never amount to anything.","\"Offer them the contract, Victoria,\" Jude commanded. \"But make sure they know exactly whose name is on the check.\"","***","Later that afternoon, the Carmichael household was dead quiet.","Chloe was sitting on the living room sofa, staring blankly at the wall.","Trent Belmont had dumped her, his family was ruined, and her dreams of marrying into high society had evaporated.","In the kitchen, Evelyn Carmichael was rubbing her temples, staring at a stack of unpaid vendor invoices.","Her event-planning business was going under... In a matter of weeks, they were going to lose the house.","Suddenly, her business phone rang.","Evelyn sighed, expecting another angry debt collector.","She picked up the receiver. \"Carmichael Events, Evelyn speaking.\"","\"Mrs. Carmichael,\" a professional female voice said. \"My name is Victoria, Senior Counsel for Apex Media Group. My client has specifically requested your firm to handle the mainland logistics for our upcoming multi-million-dollar summer gala at Sapphire Cove.\"","Evelyn dropped her pen. Her jaw fell open.","Apex Media?! Sapphire Cove?! It was a contract worth millions in pure commission! It was a miracle!","\"Yes! Absolutely!\" Evelyn screamed, tears of joy springing to her eyes. \"Oh, thank you! Thank you! Please, who is your client? I want to send him a personal gift basket!\"","There was a brief pause on the other end of the line.","\"My client,\" Victoria said, \"is Jude Lawson.\""]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21: Homeless?","paragraphs":["The landline receiver slipped from Evelyn Carmichael’s trembling fingers.","She stood frozen, her eyes wide, the color draining from her face.","Jude Lawson?","The man she had endlessly mocked for wearing cheap suits.","The man she had explicitly ordered out of her house just a few days ago, telling him he would never be worthy of her daughter.","\"Mom?\" Chloe called out from the living room, annoyed by the sudden noise. \"What did you drop?\"","Evelyn snapped out of her stupor.","A wild energy surged through her veins. She sprinted into the living room, clutching the edge of the sofa where Chloe was sulking.","\"Chloe!\" Evelyn gasped, out of breath. \"We are saved! We are going to be richer than the Belmonts!\"","Chloe looked up, her brow furrowing in confusion. \"What are you talking about? Belmont Enterprises is going bankrupt. Trent won’t even return my texts.\"","\"Forget Trent!\" Evelyn shrieked, waving her hands. \"I just received a call from the Senior Counsel of Apex Media Group! They are hiring Carmichael Events to handle the mainland logistics for a massive summer gala at Sapphire Cove! It’s a multi-million-dollar commission! And do you know who the new owner of Apex Media is?\"","Chloe blinked. \"Sapphire Cove? That’s impossible. Who?\"","Evelyn grabbed Chloe by the shoulders. \"It’s Jude! Jude Lawson!\"","Chloe’s heart stopped.","Jude?","The viral videos, the rumors floating around the city about a mysterious new billionaire, the sudden collapse of Trent’s family business... it all clicked into place.","Jude was the titan the entire city had been whispering about!","\"He... he’s a billionaire?\" Chloe whispered, a sudden wave of nausea washing over her as she realized what she had thrown away.","\"Don’t you see what this means, Chloe?!\" Evelyn laughed, pacing the living room. \"He bought an entertainment empire and an exclusive private island! And the very first thing he does with his power is throw a multi-million-dollar lifeline to our failing business!\"","\"He’s giving us the contract,\" Chloe murmured, a smug smile creeping onto her face.","\"Exactly!\" Evelyn clapped her hands together. \"He is still obsessed with you! He’s throwing his millions at us because he’s desperate for your forgiveness! He probably hid his wealth to test you, and now he realizes he can’t survive without you.\"","Chloe felt a surge of power.","Trent had dumped her, leaving her feeling worthless, but now?","The most powerful man in the city was crawling back to her doorstep, handing her family millions of dollars just to get her attention!","\"I always knew he had potential,\" Chloe said, tossing her hair over her shoulder. \"I’ll make him apologize for putting me through all this stress, of course. But once we are back together, the Carmichael family will practically own this city. We don’t need the Belmonts at all.\"","\"Oh, we are going to be royalty,\" Evelyn agreed. \"Go put on some makeup! His lawyer is coming over right now to finalize the paperwork!\"","Thirty minutes later, a black corporate SUV pulled up to the curb outside the Carmichael residence.","Evelyn was already standing by the front door, wearing her most expensive dress.","When Victoria Vance stepped out of the vehicle holding a leather briefcase, Evelyn threw the door open and rushed down the walkway, beaming as if she were greeting an old friend.","\"Welcome, welcome!\" Evelyn gushed, extending both hands. \"Please, come inside! Can I get you some tea? Or perhaps champagne? We are just so thrilled!\"","Victoria offered a nod and stepped past the older woman into the house.","Chloe was waiting in the living room, sitting on the sofa with perfect posture, wearing a designer dress she couldn’t actually afford.","She offered Victoria a knowing smile.","\"Please, Ms. Vance, have a seat,\" Chloe said smoothly. \"And you can tell Jude he didn’t need to be so formal with his lawyers. We are family. I am more than willing to speak with him directly.\"","Victoria stopped in the center of the living room.","She placed her briefcase onto the coffee table and popped the golden latches.","\"Mrs. Carmichael. Miss Carmichael,\" Victoria said. \"I believe you have misunderstood the nature of this transaction.\"","Evelyn’s smile faltered. \"I’m sorry?\"","\"Mr. Lawson is not your family,\" Victoria corrected bluntly, pulling a stack of contracts from the briefcase. \"And he has no interest in speaking with you, nor does he possess any lingering affection for you. He did not select your firm out of a desire for reconciliation.\"","Chloe felt the smug confidence drain from her body, replaced by a sudden knot of dread. \"Then... why is he giving us the contract?\"","\"He selected Carmichael Events because he required a local vendor desperate enough to accept his specific operational terms without negotiation,\" Victoria stated, laying the contract flat on the table and handing Evelyn a pen.","Evelyn swallowed hard, her hands shaking slightly as she looked down at the paper. \"What... what operational terms?\"","Victoria adjusted her glasses, looking down at the two women with pity.","\"The commission structure outlined in Section Four is incredibly generous,\" Victoria explained. \"Upon completion, your firm will be paid three million dollars. It is more than enough to clear your vendor debts and save this house from foreclosure.\"","Evelyn let out a breath she didn’t realize she was holding.","Three million dollars... They were saved.","\"However,\" Victoria continued, her voice hardening, \"Section Five outlines the performance requirements. As the contracted mainland logistics team, Carmichael Events is strictly prohibited from stepping foot on the corporate jets or Sapphire Cove.\"","Chloe frowned. \"Wait, we aren’t invited to the gala?\"","\"You are not guests, Miss Carmichael,\" Victoria said, her tone razor-sharp. \"You are the service staff. Mr. Lawson explicitly required that the owners of Carmichael Events must facilitate the mainland boarding process.\"","\"You will be standing on the tarmac for eight hours,\" Victoria detailed, locking eyes with Chloe. \"You will be unloading the luggage of the Apex Media executives. You will be checking coats, tagging bags, and parking the cars of the A-list actresses who *are* invited to the island.\"","\"He wants me to be a baggage handler?!\" Chloe shrieked, jumping up from the sofa. \"For a party I’m not even allowed to attend?! I won’t do it! I refuse!\"","Evelyn looked like she was going to be sick.","Jude wasn’t trying to win them back...","He was forcing them into manual labor to serve his new elite social circle, purely to humiliate them.","\"You are free to refuse the contract,\" Victoria said, closing her empty briefcase and snapping the latches shut. \"If you do not accept this three-million-dollar lifeline today, Carmichael Events will file for Chapter 11 bankruptcy on Friday. The bank will seize this house by the end of the month.\"","Victoria stepped away from the table, walking toward the front door.","She paused in the entryway, looking back at the devastated mother and daughter.","\"Mr. Lawson wanted to ensure that you both got a front-row seat to the lifestyle you threw away,\" Victoria said. \"Sign the contract, or lose your house. The choice is yours.\"","Victoria walked out the front door.","Evelyn stared at the contract sitting on her coffee table.","Just five minutes ago, she had believed this piece of paper was a golden ticket...","A romantic plea from a billionaire begging to be let back into their family.","She had thought Carmichael Events was selected because of her stellar reputation in the local community.","\"Mom,\" Chloe whispered, her voice trembling as she sank back down onto the sofa, burying her face in her hands. \"I can’t do it. I can’t stand on a dock in a uniform and carry luggage for A-list actresses. The paparazzi will be there! If anyone recognizes me, I’ll be a laughingstock!\"","Evelyn’s hands were shaking.","She looked around the beautifully decorated living room, at the imported chandeliers and the expensive furniture she had bought on credit.","If she didn’t sign this contract, all of it would be auctioned off by the bank in less than thirty days.","She would be homeless.","\"We don’t have a choice,\" Evelyn croaked, her throat bone-dry.","She picked up the expensive fountain pen Victoria had left on the table.","With a trembling hand, Evelyn signed her name on the dotted line, binding herself and her daughter to act as manual laborers for the man she had thrown out of her house like garbage.","When she finished signing, Evelyn dropped the pen. It rolled off the table and hit the carpet.","\"How could he do this?\" Evelyn muttered. \"He’s just an employee! Trent said it himself! Jude is just a broke loser who got hired as a frontman for a viral marketing stunt!\"","Chloe looked up, her makeup slightly smeared from her tears. \"Mom... Trent’s family is bankrupt. Jude bought Zenith Motors out from under them.\"","\"He didn’t buy anything!\" Evelyn shrieked in denial, pacing the room. \"Don’t you see, Chloe? This is just some new corporate boss pulling strings! Jude probably begged his employer to give us this contract just so he could lord it over us. He’s abusing whatever little scrap of authority his boss gave him!\"","Evelyn stopped pacing, her eyes lighting up with a spark of hope.","\"That’s it!\" Evelyn gasped, clapping her hands together. \"When we get to the dock next week, you can talk to his real boss. You can explain that Jude is using company funds to carry out a petty personal vendetta against his ex-fiancée. We can get Jude fired, and maybe his boss will take an interest in you!\"","Chloe stared at her mother, feeling a sudden knot of dread forming in the pit of her stomach.","She couldn’t accept that a kid in a cheap suit was now a titan...","But Chloe wasn’t so sure anymore.","Victoria was a Senior Partner at one of the most ruthless corporate law firms on the East Coast.","Women like her didn’t act as errand runners for \"proxies\" or low-level employees.","\"Mom... stop,\" Chloe whispered, her hands shaking as she pulled her smartphone out of her designer purse.","\"I’m telling you, Chloe, this is our chance to expose him!\" Evelyn continued, ignoring her daughter. \"We just need to find out who really owns Apex Media Group! Once we find the real billionaire, we—\"","\"I said stop!\" Chloe yelled, her voice cracking.","Evelyn flinched, staring at her daughter in shock. \"Chloe, what is wrong with you?\""]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22: Sole Shareholder","paragraphs":["Chloe didn’t answer. Her fingers were flying across her phone’s screen.","She bypassed Google and logged directly into the state’s official corporate registry database... the same public database the Belmonts used to track their competitors.","Her heart hammered against her ribs as she typed in the search bar: *Apex Media Group*.","The page loaded.","Chloe’s breath hitched in her throat. She scrolled down past the corporate address and the tax identifiers, straight to the section listing the board of directors and the majority shareholders.","There was only one name listed.","*Sole Shareholder (100% Equity): Jude Lawson.*","She couldn’t breathe. Her vision blurred for a second.","She quickly typed a new search into the database: *Zenith Motors Parent Holdings.*","The page loaded instantly.","*Majority Shareholder (78% Equity): Jude Lawson.*","The phone slipped from Chloe’s hands, landing with a soft thud on the plush living room carpet.","\"Chloe?\" Evelyn asked, taking a hesitant step forward. \"What is it? What did you find? Who is the real owner?\"","Chloe looked up at her mother. A single tear spilled over her eyelashes, ruining her carefully applied mascara.","\"There is no boss, Mom,\" Chloe whispered.","Evelyn frowned, confusion masking the rising panic in her chest. \"What do you mean there’s no boss? Of course there is. Who owns the companies?\"","\"Jude,\" Chloe choked out, a sob finally breaking through her throat. \"Jude owns them. He owns all of it.\"","\"That’s impossible!\" Evelyn snapped, marching over and snatching the phone off the carpet. \"You’re reading it wrong! The internet is full of fake rumors—\"","Evelyn looked down at the screen. She recognized the official seal of the state registry at the top of the page.","This was a legally binding, government-verified financial document.","She stared at the name. *Jude Lawson.*","Evelyn felt the blood drain entirely from her head. Her legs instantly turned to jelly. She collapsed backward, her knees hitting the carpet.","\"No...\" Evelyn gasped. \"No, no, no... he was a car washer. He couldn’t even afford the deposit on the catering hall...\"","She had stood in this exact living room and screamed at Jude, telling him he was a failure who would drag her daughter into poverty.","She had shoved him out the front door so Chloe could chase after Trent Belmont... a boy whose family Jude had bankrupted just days later.","And because of Evelyn’s arrogance, instead of being the mother-in-law to a billionaire, she was now legally contractually obligated to carry his guests’ luggage.","Evelyn buried her face in her hands, letting out a pathetic, devastating wail of regret.","***","Miles away, the black Maybach rolled through the private gates of the Obsidian Grand Hotel, pulling to a silent stop near the VIP elevators.","Jude sat in the cabin, holding a glass of sparkling water.","He looked out the tinted window at the city skyline, a faint smile touching his lips.","By now, Victoria would have delivered the contract to the Carmichaels.","He knew Evelyn well enough to know she would sign it...","Her pride was massive, but her fear of poverty was much, much stronger.","She would take the three million dollars, and she would stand on that dock in a service uniform.","Jude took a slow sip of his water. .","\"I hope you brought comfortable shoes, Evelyn,\" Jude murmured to himself, setting the glass down.","The driver opened the door, and Jude stepped out into the afternoon air.","It was time to head up to the Presidential Suite and prepare for the next phase of his empire’s expansion.","The Sapphire Cove gala was going to be an event the city would never forget...","[Ding!]","[Hidden Mission Triggered: Understated Dominance.]","[Objective: The true charm of a financial titan is exercising absolute power without the need to boast. Casually deploy superior assets to completely shatter a rival’s prestige.]","[Reward: +2 Money Sign-Ins, +1 Platinum System Reward Box!]","Jude smiled.","The system was basically telling him to act like he’d been doing this his entire life.","There was no need to yell or flex; true wealth spoke for itself ..","He walked through the sliding glass doors into the main VIP lounge.","The terminal was a sprawling sanctuary designed explicitly for the ultra-rich, featuring private barista bars, plush leather seating, and floor-to-ceiling windows overlooking the tarmac.","The lounge was currently buzzing with the most famous faces in the country. The top executives, A-list actresses, and directors of Apex Media Group were mingling, sipping mimosas and laughing as they prepared for the company’s summer gala.","But Jude’s eyes immediately drifted toward the luggage drop-off area near the doors.","Standing there, wearing identically humiliating, gray service uniforms, were Chloe and Evelyn Carmichael.","They were both sweating, struggling to hoist an oversized designer trunk onto a brass luggage cart.","Chloe’s face was beet red, her hair pulled back into a messy ponytail.","Every time a famous actress walked past and handed her a garment bag without even looking at her, Chloe looked like she wanted the marble floor to open up and swallow her whole.","Evelyn wasn’t faring any better...","The woman who had once prided herself on hosting elite tea parties was currently being scolded by a twenty-two-year-old pop star for accidentally scuffing a leather suitcase.","Jude watched them suffer for a few moments, feeling a quiet satisfaction. They were getting exactly what they had earned.","Before Jude could approach his executives, the double doors of the terminal swung open, and a loud, obnoxiously familiar voice echoed through the lounge.","\"Make sure the VIP tags are on those bags! We have a connection to catch!\"","Donovan Pierce, the arrogant heir to Pierce Studios, strutted into the lounge.","Trailing behind him were about twenty actors and actresses who had signed with his studio.","Donovan was clutching a stack of boarding passes, looking incredibly smug.","Donovan scanned the room and locked eyes with Jude.","A wide grin spread across the heir’s face as he marched straight over.","\"Well, well, well,\" Donovan laughed, holding up his stack of boarding passes like a trophy. \"If it isn’t the new owner of Apex Media. I didn’t expect to see you at the private terminal, Lawson. I figured you’d be bussing your talent down to the public airport.\"","Jude took a sip from a glass of water a waiter had just handed him. \"Morning, Donovan.\"","\"My father booked us all first-class commercial tickets down to Miami,\" Donovan boasted, ensuring the Apex Media actresses nearby could hear him. \"From there, we are boarding a two-hundred-foot mega-yacht that will sail us straight to Sapphire Cove. It’s going to take half a day, but the luxury is unparalleled.\"","Donovan looked around the lounge, pretending to search for something. \"So, where is your ride? Let me guess, you chartered a little twin-engine prop plane? A cramped little Cessna to squeeze your A-listers into? Be careful, Lawson, those cheap rental jets get awfully turbulent over the ocean.\"","Seraphina Frost, the acting CEO of Apex Media, walked up beside Jude, glaring at Donovan.","\"Pierce, you are embarrassing yourself. This is a private terminal lounge. Go wait at your commercial gate.\"","\"Oh, don’t be bitter, Seraphina,\" Donovan sneered. \"I just want to make sure your talent knows what they are missing out on.\"","Jude checked his platinum Audemars Piguet, his expression bored.","\"I don’t charter planes, Donovan,\" Jude said, his voice quiet, yet somehow carrying across the entire lounge.","Donovan frowned, his smile faltering slightly. \"What do you mean you don’t charter?\"","\"I mean, I own my fleet,\" Jude replied.","He gestured with his glass toward the floor-to-ceiling windows overlooking the primary runway. \"And I certainly wouldn’t put my talent in a Cessna.\"","Donovan turned his head to look out the window. Every actress and executive in the lounge followed his gaze.","Rolling slowly and silently out of the private hangar, guided by a team of ground crew in neon vests, was a modified, custom-retrofitted Boeing 787 Dreamliner.","The aircraft was painted a sleek, reflective midnight black, with the Apex Media Group logo embossed in subtle platinum lettering along the fuselage.","The entire lounge went dead silent. Even the Apex Media actresses, who were used to traveling in high-end luxury, gasped in shock.","\"I... I must have misheard you,\" Donovan stammered, the color draining from his face as he stared up at the towering jet. \"That... that’s a commercial airliner. You can’t privately own a Dreamliner!\"","\"It was retrofitted for fifty passengers,\" Jude explained, turning his attention back to his water. \"It has master suites, a full dining room, and a cinema. It’s a bit excessive for a two-hour flight to the Caribbean, but I prefer my staff to travel comfortably.\"","Donovan swallowed hard, his throat clicking audibly in the quiet room.","He looked down at the stack of first-class Delta tickets in his hand. Just thirty seconds ago, he thought those tickets were the ultimate flex.","Now, compared to a private, custom-built Boeing 787, they looked like cheap bus passes.","The Pierce Studios actors standing behind Donovan groaned. They looked out the window at Jude’s flying palace, then glared at Donovan with jealousy.","\"We have to fly commercial and sit on a boat for eight hours,\" a famous leading man muttered angrily to Donovan. \"And they get to take a private Dreamliner?\"","\"Shut up!\" Donovan hissed, humiliated.","Over by the luggage carts, Chloe Carmichael watched the entire exchange.","She leaned against a brass pole.","That plane belonged to the man she had called a broke loser.","If she hadn’t listened to her mother, she would be boarding that flying palace as his fiancée, rather than loading suitcases into its cargo hold.","[Ding!]","[Mission Completed: Understated Dominance.]","[Reward: +2 Money Sign-Ins, +1 Platinum System Reward Box.]","Jude smiled as the system chime rang in his head.","\"Ladies and gentlemen,\" Jude announced to his stunned executives and talent. \"The crew has finalized the pre-flight checks. Please proceed to the boarding bridge. We have an island to get to.\"","The Apex Media team erupted into cheers, completely ignoring Donovan as they eagerly made their way toward the private boarding tunnel.","Ten minutes later, Jude stepped into the main cabin of the Dreamliner...","It was even more spectacular than the blueprints had suggested.","The interior had been gutted and replaced with plush leather lounge seating, a bar, and warm, ambient lighting.","Beautiful flight attendants in tailored uniforms were already handing out flutes of vintage champagne to the guests.","\"Mr. Lawson!\" one of the lead actresses cheered, raising her glass as he walked in. \"Who even cares about the private island anymore? I could live on this plane for the rest of my life!\"","Jude chuckled, taking a seat in a recliner at the front of the cabin.","\"Enjoy the flight,\" Jude said, looking out the window.","He called up the system interface with a flick of his mind. \"Sign in.\""]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23: Mission","paragraphs":["[Bonus Sign-In 1 Successful! Reward: $30,000,000 USD.]","[Bonus Sign-In 2 Successful! Reward: $40,000,000 USD.]","The banking notifications flashed across his lock screen, confirming that seventy million dollars of liquid cash had just been deposited into his offshore accounts.","Despite its size, the custom Dreamliner ascended into the coastal sky with zero turbulence.","The transition was so smooth that the champagne sitting in Jude’s crystal flute didn’t even ripple.","\"This is incredible,\" one of the younger pop stars murmured, looking around the cabin. \"I’ve flown private a dozen times, but it always feels like you’re bouncing around in a tin can. I can’t even tell we’re moving!\"","\"That’s the beauty of a retrofitted commercial chassis,\" Seraphina Frost said, sinking into the recliner across from Jude with a sigh. \"Mr. Lawson spared no expense. This is the pinnacle of aviation luxury.\"","The cabin was filled with the sound of cheerful laughter.","Jude watched his new employees enjoy themselves, feeling a quiet satisfaction.","He had completed the ’Understated Dominance’ objective simply by bringing them on board.","But the system wasn’t finished with him just yet.","[Ding!]","[Continuous Mission Triggered: Absolute High-Profile Dominance!]","[Objective: Understated elegance has its place, but true financial titans must occasionally shatter the paradigms of those around them. Execute a high-profile display of overwhelming wealth to secure absolute loyalty.]","[Reward: +1 Money Sign-In, +1 Diamond System Reward Box!]","Jude raised an eyebrow. The system wanted him to go loud.","Another Diamond Box was an incredibly rare reward... the last one had given him absolute probability and a sovereign island.","If the system was demanding a high-profile flex to earn it, Jude was more than happy to oblige...","He didn’t have to wait long for an opportunity.","A tall man in his late fifties walked up the aisle from the rear lounge area, carrying a digital tablet.","It was Richard Sterling, the Chief Financial Officer of Apex Media Group.","Richard paused beside Jude’s recliner, adjusting his glasses. He looked impressed by the plane.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" Richard said. \"I must admit, this aircraft is a masterpiece. However, as your CFO, I have a fiduciary duty to ask about the company’s current burn rate.\"","Jude took a sip of his champagne. \"Go on, Richard.\"","\"It’s regarding Sapphire Cove,\" Richard explained, tapping his tablet to pull up a spreadsheet. \"I know Donovan Pierce was bragging back at the terminal, but Pierce Studios actually did manage to secure a temporary rental for two acres of beachfront on the edge of the island. It cost them fifty million dollars just for a four-day permit.\"","Seraphina frowned. \"Fifty million for two acres? That’s extortionate.\"","\"It’s Sapphire Cove,\" Richard countered. \"It is the most isolated paradise in the world. Which brings me to my point, Mr. Lawson. I need to know how much of the island you rented for our summer gala, so I can balance the quarterly ledger. If we rented a larger plot than Pierce Studios, the financial hit could disrupt our Q3 earnings.\"","The ambient conversation in the front of the cabin slowly died down.","Several of the A-list actresses and top directors leaned in, suddenly very interested in the logistics of their destination.","Jude swirled the champagne in his glass.","\"You don’t need to balance anything, Richard,\" Jude said.","Richard blinked. \"Sir? I don’t understand. The rental fees for the island must be accounted for in the corporate registry, otherwise we risk an audit.\"","\"There are no rental fees,\" Jude said.","A murmur of confusion rippled through the actresses.","Had he cheaped out? Were they not actually staying on the island?","Jude looked directly into Richard’s anxious eyes.","\"I don’t rent real estate, Richard,\" Jude stated. \"I own Sapphire Cove. The entire island. All five hundred acres, as well as the exclusive, sovereign maritime rights to the ten square nautical miles of ocean surrounding it.\"","Richard’s jaw dropped. The tablet slipped from his fingers.","\"You... you own it?\" Richard stammered. \"The entire island?\"","\"Yes,\" Jude smiled faintly. \"So you can delete that spreadsheet.\"","Richard’s eyes went wide as he calculated the math out loud.","\"Pierce Studios paid fifty million dollars to rent two acres for a weekend,\" Richard muttered, grabbing his head. \"If you own all five hundred acres... plus the sovereign sea rights... that’s... that’s a five-billion-dollar acquisition! At a minimum! And that’s assuming you could even bypass the international treaties required to purchase sovereign land!\"","Five billion dollars?","The A-list actresses, who were used to dating millionaires and attending lavish Hollywood parties, suddenly realized how incredibly small their world actually was.","The man sitting in front of them hadn’t just rented a party venue; he had dropped five billion dollars to purchase a fortress just to host a summer retreat!","\"Oh my god,\" Chloe, the lead actress, whispered, pressing her hands against her cheeks. \"We are going to a private, five-billion-dollar island.\"","The actresses were screaming in excitement. The directors were laughing in disbelief, pouring more champagne and toasting to Jude’s name...","They had forgotten about Pierce Studios.","Donovan Pierce’s fifty-million-dollar rental was an absolute joke compared to Jude owning the entire landmass.","Richard, the cynical CFO, slowly sank into an empty chair, staring at Jude.","\"I... I apologize for questioning the budget, Mr. Lawson,\" Richard whispered. \"Your liquidity is beyond my comprehension.\"","Jude smiled, turning his gaze back out the window.","The system chime rang in his mind.","[Mission Completed: Absolute High-Profile Dominance!]","[Reward: +1 Money Sign-In, +1 Diamond System Reward Box!]","The rest of the two-and-a-half-hour flight passed in a blur of celebration.","The Apex Media executives and talent were riding an unbelievable high, treating Jude with a level of worship usually reserved for royalty.","As the Dreamliner began its final descent, the turquoise waters of the Caribbean came into view.","Jude looked down through the glass.","Sapphire Cove was breathtaking...","A massive expanse of lush green jungle, white sand beaches, and blue lagoons sprawled out below them.","The jet banked smoothly, lining up with a two-mile-long private runway that cut through the center of the tropical paradise.","As the jet taxied toward the private island terminal, the passengers crowded the windows, pointing and gasping in awe.","Waiting on the tarmac was a fleet of stretched, luxury golf carts and sleek black SUVs.","Standing at attention in front of the vehicles was a line of over fifty uniformed staff members.","At the head of the line stood a silver-haired man in a white linen suit... the island’s elite estate manager.","As the boarding stairs were lowered and Jude stepped out into the tropical sun, the staff bowed deeply.","\"Welcome to Sapphire Cove, Mr. Lawson,\" the estate manager called out. \"Your island is ready.\""]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24: The Studio","paragraphs":["While the Apex Media executives and A-list celebrities were busy settling into the unparalleled luxury of Sapphire Cove, Jude’s mind was already moving on to his next maneuver...","He had stayed on the island just long enough to ensure the gala was operating flawlessly before boarding the Dreamliner and flying straight back to the mainland.","At that exact moment, on the other side of the city, a young woman named Harper was standing outside the gates of Apex Studios.","Harper was twenty-two, fiercely creative, and had spent the last three years getting her indie film scripts repeatedly rejected by every major studio in the city.","Just yesterday, Jude had accidentally bumped into her at a downtown coffee shop while she was sketching storyboards.","Guided by his *Absolute Appraisal* skill Jude had made a decision.","He had appointed Harper as the new President of Original Content for Apex Studios.","True to her indie roots, Harper hadn’t bothered to buy a corporate pantsuit.","She showed up for her first day wearing a vintage denim jacket, a faded band t-shirt, and scuffed boots.","As Harper walked through the front doors of the studio’s main administrative building, she immediately ran into a familiar face.","It was Gregory, a senior executive producer at Apex.","Gregory was an arrogant gatekeeper who had thrown Harper’s scripts into the trash on three separate occasions, once telling her she had the creative depth of a puddle.","Gregory was sipping an espresso when he spotted her. He nearly choked on his drink.","\"You have got to be kidding me,\" Gregory sneered, marching over to block her path. \"How did you get past the front gate? I told you last month, we do not accept unsolicited garbage from amateurs.\"","Harper stood her ground, her jaw tightening. \"I’m not here to drop off a script, Gregory.\"","\"Oh, really?\" Gregory laughed, a mocking sound. \"Let me guess, you’re here to beg for a job as a production assistant? Go fetch coffee somewhere else. This is a multi-billion-dollar studio, not a charity for failed art students. Security is going to drag you out of here in about thirty seconds.\"","\"Actually, I’m here to work,\" Harper said, keeping her voice calm.","Gregory rolled his eyes. \"Work? You? Did you forge a security badge? Because I oversee all departmental hires, and I would sooner burn this building to the ground than let you anywhere near a soundstage.\"","\"Please, step aside!\"","A voice echoed across the lobby.","The studio’s Director of Human Resources, a sharply dressed woman clutching a clipboard, was sprinting toward them. She looked out of breath.","\"I am so incredibly sorry for the delay, Madam President,\" the HR Director gasped, ignoring Gregory as she bowed her head toward Harper. \"I should have been waiting for you at the gate.\"","Gregory froze.","\"Madam... President?\" Gregory choked out, looking between the HR Director and the girl in the denim jacket.","\"It’s fine, Sarah,\" Harper smiled at the HR Director.","She then turned her gaze back to Gregory, offering a knowing look. \"I’ll see you in the boardroom, Gregory. Try not to be late.\"","Harper walked past him, following the HR Director toward the executive elevators.","The girl he had just mocked was the new President of Original Content?","How was that even possible?","Ten minutes later, inside the executive boardroom, Harper sat at the head of the table.","The studio’s veteran executives were seated around her, their faces barely concealing their disdain.","The news of her appointment had spread like wildfire, and none of them were happy about answering to a twenty-two-year-old girl in a denim jacket.","Gregory, having recovered a fraction of his bravado, sat directly across from her. He cleared his throat.","\"Madam President, since you are so eager to work, we actually have a major creative deadlock that requires your immediate sign-off,\" Gregory said.","\"I’m listening,\" Harper said, opening her notebook.","\"We have a hundred-million-dollar budget allocated for our Q4 flagship release,\" Gregory explained, leaning forward. \"The board is split between two projects. Project A is a high-octane superhero sequel. It’s safe, it has built-in merchandise, and it guarantees a box office return. Project B is a sci-fi thriller. It’s original, extremely dark, and incredibly niche. Which one are we greenlighting?\"","Harper’s eyes lit up. This was exactly why Jude had hired her!","\"The superhero market is oversaturated,\" Harper said confidently, tapping her pen against the table. \"Audiences are experiencing fatigue with generic sequels. The sci-fi thriller is a risk, yes, but it allows for ground-breaking creative direction. It pushes the medium forward. We greenlight the thriller.\"","The boardroom descended into mocking silence.","A few of the older executives exchanged amused glances. Gregory let out a sigh.","\"With all due respect, Madam President,\" Gregory said, openly sneering now. \"You have no understanding of the market. Originality doesn’t pay the bills. A superhero sequel is a guaranteed billion-dollar IP. A niche thriller is a financial black hole. If we follow your direction, the studio will lose tens of millions.\"","The other executives nodded in agreement.","\"The girl doesn’t know what she’s doing,\" a senior marketing VP muttered under his breath, just loud enough for her to hear.","Harper felt her face flush hot with humiliation.","She was the President, but she had zero actual authority in this room...","They were humiliating her to prove she didn’t belong.","Before Harper could attempt to defend her position, her cell phone buzzed on the table.","It was a text from Jude Lawson.","*How is the first day going?*","Harper quickly typed back, her fingers shaking slightly: *Not great. The board is stonewalling me on my first greenlight. They think I’m a joke.*","Jude’s reply was instantaneous: *I’m in the lobby.*","Harper let out a sigh of relief. She stood up from the table. \"Excuse me for a moment. We will resume this discussion shortly.\"","Down in the main lobby, Jude was admiring the movie posters lining the walls.","Having just flown back from Sapphire Cove, he was dressed in relaxed trousers and an unbuttoned shirt.","Gregory, who had stepped out of the boardroom to grab another espresso, spotted Jude near the elevators.","Gregory was already in a foul mood from dealing with Harper, and seeing a guy in beachwear loitering in the executive lobby pushed him over the edge.","\"Hey, you!\" Gregory barked, marching over to Jude. \"What do you think you’re doing? The holding pens for background extras are in Building C. Get out of the executive lobby before I have you banned from the lot.\"","Jude turned around. He looked at Gregory with an unimpressed expression.","\"I don’t think you have the authority to ban me,\" Jude said softly.","\"I am the Senior Executive Producer of this studio!\" Gregory yelled, his face turning red. \"I can have you blacklisted from the entire industry! Now get out of here, you cheap—\"","Jude raised his left hand to check his phone.","As he did, the sleeve of his shirt slid back, exposing his wrist.","The overhead lobby lights caught the brilliant gleam of a platinum, diamond-encrusted Audemars Piguet Royal Oak.","It was a custom timepiece that retailed for well over half a million dollars...","Gregory’s tirade died instantly in his throat.","His eyes locked onto the watch.","A guy wearing cheap linen didn’t sport an AP Royal Oak unless the linen was bespoke and the casualness was a byproduct of untouchable wealth.","\"Mr. Lawson!\"","Harper’s voice rang out across the lobby as she jogged out of the elevator banks.","She threw her arms around Jude, relieved to see her only ally.","Gregory felt his legs turn to jelly. The new President was hugging this guy...","\"Madam President,\" Gregory stammered. \"Who... who is this gentleman?\"","Harper pulled back, offering Gregory a smile.","\"Gregory, allow me to introduce you to the man who signed your paychecks,\" Harper said. \"This is Jude Lawson. He owns the studio.\""]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25: Pocket Change","paragraphs":["Gregory looked as if all the oxygen had just been sucked out of the room.","He stared at the half-million-dollar platinum Audemars Piguet resting on Jude’s wrist, and then up at Jude’s calm expression.","He had just threatened to have the billionaire owner of the studio thrown into the background extra holding pens...","Jude didn’t even bother to fire him. He looked at Harper and said, \"If he gives you any more trouble with your creative greenlights, terminate his contract and blacklist him from the lot.\"","With that, Jude turned and walked out of the executive lobby.","Jude had promised the Apex Media executives a legendary summer gala, and he fully intended to deliver.","His Dreamliner was already waiting at the private mainland airstrip, fully fueled and ready to take him straight back to his tropical empire.","By the time the late afternoon sun began to cast shadows over the waters of the Caribbean, Jude’s bare feet were sinking into the sands of Sapphire Cove.","The beach was transformed into a paradise...","As Jude approached the main gathering near the shoreline, he noticed a distinct disruption.","A speedboat had beached itself near the cabanas, and a group of men in swimwear had crashed the private party.","At the center of the group was a blonde European man who was flirting with Seraphina Frost and several of the lead actresses.","\"Mr. Lawson,\" the island’s estate manager murmured, stepping up beside Jude. \"I apologize for the intrusion. That is Sebastian Thorne. He is the heir to a European shipping conglomerate that owns a much smaller, secondary atoll a few miles east of here. Should I have security remove them?\"","Before Jude could answer, a familiar chime echoed in his mind.","[Ding!]","[Continuous Mission Triggered: Financial Overkill.]","[Objective: An interloper is attempting to leverage his wealth to poach your guests and undermine your prestige. Obliterate his net worth in a single transaction.]","[Reward: +2 Money Sign-Ins, +1 Platinum System Reward Box!]","Jude smiled faintly. \"No. Let him speak. I want to see exactly what he thinks he’s doing.\"","Jude walked closer, slipping into the crowd of executives just in time to hear Sebastian Thorne’s loud pitch.","\"A beach party is incredibly quaint, ladies, but it’s just sand,\" Sebastian boasted. \"I, on the other hand, am not short on capital. I am currently spending twenty million dollars to lease the offshore coral reefs for the evening, and I have chartered a fleet of twenty private yachts to take us out there. Leave this boring retreat and come party on the open ocean with me!\"","A few of the younger actresses exchanged wide-eyed glances.","\"Twenty million dollars?\" one of the pop stars whispered, genuinely shocked. \"He’s spending twenty million just for a sunset party?\"","\"Renting twenty private yachts requires hiring professional maritime crews for each vessel,\" one of Sebastian’s European friends bragged. \"And leasing public reefs for a private event costs a fortune in government permits. Sebastian doesn’t care. He throws around twenty million like it’s pocket change!\"","Sebastian puffed his chest out, clearly feeding off the awe and hesitation of the Apex Media talent.","He looked around the beach.","\"So,\" Sebastian smirked, offering his hand to Seraphina. \"Who wants to board my speedboat and head to the yachts?\"","\"Nobody is getting on your boat, Sebastian,\" a calm voice echoed across the sand.","The crowd parted as Jude stepped forward.","Sebastian frowned, looking Jude up and down. \"And who are you supposed to be? The event planner?\"","\"I’m the owner,\" Jude replied. He let out a soft laugh. \"And I have to say, Sebastian, I find your attempt to lease the coral reefs incredibly amusing.\"","Sebastian’s face hardened. \"Amusing? I just dropped twenty million dollars. What could possibly be amusing about that?\"","\"Because you can’t lease those reefs,\" Jude said, gesturing toward the waters stretching out to the horizon. \"The ten square nautical miles of ocean surrounding this island is not public water. It falls within my sovereign exclusion zone. It is my private territory. You couldn’t lease it if you offered me a billion dollars.\"","The crowd of actresses gasped.","Sebastian’s smirk instantly vanished.","He looked out at the ocean, his face turning pale.","Sovereign maritime rights?","That was a level of wealth that his shipping family couldn’t even dream of acquiring...","But Jude wasn’t finished. The system had demanded overkill, and Jude was more than happy to bury the interloper.","Jude turned slightly, snapping his fingers to get the attention of his estate manager.","\"Cancel Sebastian’s little rental,\" Jude commanded. \"I want thirty private yachts brought to my docks immediately. Furthermore, charter a fully staffed, hundred-person luxury ocean liner and anchor it just outside the reef.\"","The estate manager bowed. \"Right away, Mr. Lawson. Shall I secure the routing permits?\"","\"Yes,\" Jude smiled. \"In fact, go ahead and contact the international maritime authority. I want to lease the next ten square nautical miles of international waters just so my guests have extra room to race the yachts.\"","The beach fell into silence.","The executives, the actresses, and even Sebastian’s own European entourage stared at Jude as if he had just rearranged the stars in the sky.","\"You’re lying!\" Sebastian yelled, his voice cracking. \"Do you have any idea how much that costs?! A luxury hundred-person ocean liner is five million dollars a day! Thirty private yachts with professional crews will run you fifteen million! And an expedited, same-day lease for ten miles of international waters is at least ten million dollars!\"","Sebastian pointed a shaking finger at Jude. \"That is thirty million dollars for a single evening! No one spends thirty million dollars on a sunset cruise!\"","\"The funds have already cleared the international registry, Mr. Thorne,\" the estate manager interrupted, holding up a digital tablet that displayed a multi-million-dollar wire transfer receipt from Jude’s offshore account.","Sebastian stared at the green text on the tablet. His jaw went slack.","The man standing in front of him had just dropped thirty million dollars simply to prove a point...","\"Thirty million dollars for one night...\" one of Sebastian’s friends muttered. \"My god... Sebastian’s trust fund is pennies compared to this guy.\"","Without another word, Sebastian’s own entourage abandoned him, blending into the crowd of Apex Media executives who were already cheering and raising their champagne glasses to Jude.","Sebastian stood alone on the sand, humiliated.","[Ding!]","[Mission Completed: Financial Overkill.]","[Reward: +2 Money Sign-Ins, +1 Platinum System Reward Box!]","Jude smiled, looking at the actresses who were giddy with excitement at the prospect of boarding a private ocean liner.","\"The ocean liner will be here shortly,\" Jude announced, his voice welcoming. \"In the meantime, the bar is open. Enjoy yourselves.\""]}]);
